{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway","id":327030,"title":"Why should I play a Dragon-Blooded anyway ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-01T08:37:33-08:00","id":327030,"title":"Why should I play a Dragon-Blooded anyway ?","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/imagejpg1-36.jpg~original\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> <br /> It's seem that I like pretty much every splat except for Dragon-Blooded (and Lunar) who I just don't feel anything for. Their pre-errata charmset is just horrendous, post-errata improve them a bit, but there are only a few charm that catch my attention (One Mind Within,<br /> <br /> I don't find the Realm/Lookshy/Immaculate Order interesting at all, and neither are the discussion involving these subject, threads that talked about them are just as dried as vanilla to be honest. And the whole &quot;DB are the weakest Exalted, but can still win again the Solar if he rolls bad, don't have ally, low on motes :list a bunch of disadvantage for the Solar: =&gt; DB are awesome&quot; in many &quot;Sell me on DB&quot; thread just make me so annoyed for some reason.<br /> <br /> At least they have very well-written NPCs (the worst canon NPCs prize will have to go to Abyssal).<br /> <br /> I turn on Anathema and can merrily brain-storming character for any splats, except for Dragon-Blooded (and Lunar), there must be a reason for this thought I'm not sure why. And reading the &quot;Why do you like Dragon-Blooded&quot; thread don't increase my love for them at all...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 12-14-2014, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T08:43:14-08:00","id":327056,"title":"","content":"Because you want to play a character inspired from Avatar: The Last Airbender?<br /> <br /> Because you want to play a character who can burst his abilities at every-turn without fear of a Wyld-hunt?<br /> <br /> Because you want to play within a huge group of other essence-users so you can have a Game of Thrones with elementalists?<br /> <br /> That's all I have as of now (since &quot;Playing the underdog&quot; is not your kind of game from what I can gather)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T08:54:14-08:00","id":327061,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the reason to play a dragonblooded is because it facilitates the sort of games you don't seem to be particularly interested in playing. You might just have to accept them as not being your thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T09:02:46-08:00","id":327101,"title":"","content":"You should play a Dragonblood because you can walk around casually setting things on fire and most people won't stop you - some will beg you to forgive them for whatever transgression made you decide they deserved to burn. And then you laugh at their unworthiness and enslave them.<br /> <br /> Seriously, it's the best splat for being an entitled jackass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 12-01-2014, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T09:22:17-08:00","id":327119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327101#post327101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should play a Dragonblood because you can walk around casually setting things on fire and most people won't stop you - some will beg you to forgive them for whatever transgression made you decide they deserved to burn. And then you laugh at their unworthiness and enslave them.<br /> <br /> Seriously, it's the best splat for being an entitled jackass.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because you want to play a character who can burst his abilities at every-turn without fear of a Wyld-hunt? </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I forgot about the whole using your power freely without fear. I wonder if Outcaste can have the same social protection since I'm not so keen on Dynast/Lookshy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because you want to play a character inspired from Avatar: The Last Airbender? </div> </div> </div>Eh, I remembered the devs saying something about DB not being Bender (or not making Bending a central theme for them or something like that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T09:35:04-08:00","id":327136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327119#post327119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, I forgot about the whole using your power freely without fear. I wonder if Outcaste can have the same social protection since I'm not so keen on Dynast/Lookshy.</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends where you are, probably. If some form of the Immaculate religion is dominant in your area, you can go wild. If not, you'll only have as much protection as your personal power can give you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327119#post327119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I remembered the devs saying something about DB not being Bender (or not making Bending a central theme for them or something like that).</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried and failed to make a DragonBender twice. I don't think it can be done. In 2E, at least, DB native charms don't really let you flexibly control elements like Benders do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T09:35:31-08:00","id":327137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327119#post327119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Oh yeah, I forgot about the whole using your power freely without fear. I wonder if Outcaste can have the same social protection since I'm not so keen on Dynast/Lookshy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! No one's going to call the WH if you're clearly a DB (or can fake it!), and even if they did, the hunters would just look at you, maybe tell you to tone it down a bit, and move on. If they don't offer you a job...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh, I remembered the devs saying something about DB not being Bender (or not making Bending a central theme for them or something like that). </div> </div> </div>I remember the exact opposite, with them saying that playing a DB WAS gonna be &quot;All Avatar up in here!&quot; or something like that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T09:45:53-08:00","id":327140,"title":"","content":"Re: Bending:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Q: Exalted 3rd Dragon-Blooded: can you speak to whether or not players will be able to evoke Avatar: TLA with the system as written? (nicodemus144)<br /> A: Avatar evokes Dragon-Blooded. Just throwin' that out there. That said, I plan to introduce some more iconic elemental Charms to various abilities, and probably a new series of five (tentatively) DB-only martial arts. (John M\u00f8rke) </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I love Avatar, but the original series is not exactly a sterling paragon of worldbuilding -- people are there for the characterization and voice performance and amazing fight choreography, not for the well-thought sociology on what societies run by supernatural martial artists look like. So I question the assertion that we should alter the Realm to make it more like the Fire Nation. The Realm is already an amazing fantasy society, and the ideas we have for making it even more amazing have not come from Avatar.<br /> <br /> Also the observation that benders don't have much in common with DBs is a good one. Benders are people with supernatural martial arts, but they don't have dice-adders for mundane skills that push them above human competency in damn near every field of human endeavor; they also don't live to 250 years old as a matter of course. Those two things are going to -- and do -- have way more impact on how any society with them at its center look than their ability to snap their fingers and make fire. (Stephen Lea Sheppard) </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [T]here will be martial arts and Evocations that let Dragon-Blooded have more flashy elemental powers. We are also spicing up and broadening their Charm set. But do not expect them to have a basic element-bending power or 2e Infernal style designs, because that misses the point of the humanity present in the Exalted. (John M\u00f8rke) </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T10:04:34-08:00","id":327150,"title":"","content":"I'm going to quote the best bit of advice ever given about Dragon-Blooded games because I think it can be extrapolated to some of the best advice about Exalted in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted: the Dragon-Blooded</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What Solar Exalted?</b><br /> Another valid approach is to ignore the Solar Exalted entirely, in many Dragon-Blooded stories they're unnecessary. The Realm is filled with many opportunities for adventure that have nothing to do with the Solars at all. Internecine conflict, religious debates and border clashes happen all the time - usually without the involvement of the Solars. You should never feel compelled to include any element of the setting that doesn't serve your purpose; if the addition of the Solars would upset your carefully laid series don't include them. It's just as reasonable to exclude them as it is to leave out the Guild, the Threshold or any element for which you have no use. Players usually introduce complications into stories on their own without the Storyteller's helping them. If the Solar Exalted would be another complication leave them be.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T10:14:21-08:00","id":327154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327150#post327150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to quote the best bit of advice ever given about Dragon-Blooded games because I think it can be extrapolated to some of the best advice about Exalted in general.<br /> <br /> [/QUOTE=Exalted: the Dragon-Blooded]<i>You should never feel compelled to include any element of the setting that doesn't serve your purpose; if the addition of the Solars would upset your carefully laid series don't include them. It's just as reasonable to exclude them as it is to leave out the Guild, the Threshold or any element for which you have no use. Players usually introduce complications into stories on their own without the Storyteller's helping them. If the Solar Exalted would be another complication leave them be.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> [/quote]<br /> Quoting this next time people complain about the Reclamation...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T11:25:06-08:00","id":327216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327136#post327136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I tried and failed to make a DragonBender twice. I don't think it can be done. In 2E, at least, DB native charms don't really let you flexibly control elements like Benders do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right. I always forget that Ten-Thousand Dragons is NOT the true native charm-set...then I guess you're right. I might also add that Elemental Bolt Attack seems like the stunt-charm that enables bender-y powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T11:32:44-08:00","id":327220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>[T]here will be martial arts and Evocations that let Dragon-Blooded have more flashy elemental powers. We are also spicing up and broadening their Charm set. But do not expect them to have a basic element-bending power or 2e Infernal style designs, because that misses the point of the humanity present in the Exalted. (John M\u00f8rke)</i> </div> </div> </div>Well it looks like I'll have to continue my tradition of giving DB players the <i>Affinity (Element) Control</i> Spirit Charm, then. Having elementally-empowered heroes who cannot manipulate their own element will always seem backwards and weird to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T11:34:49-08:00","id":327222,"title":"","content":"I think for actual bender-type abilities you need an elemental godblood. <br /> <br /> Actually, that's a thought. Would it be game breaking to give dragonbloods an PPE-style charm that lets them learn appropriate-aspect elemental charms as if they were an Eclipse? Or is that already a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T11:48:03-08:00","id":327266,"title":"","content":"I guess I have a strange view on it, but the way I look at it there are two main reasons to play Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> <b>1. A lower power level game:</b><br /> If you have ever tried to run an exalted game where the characters are stuck in prison or otherwise in a situation that limits them and tried to run it with Celestial exalts, it never lasts that long just due to the shear power level of the charms involved. You would have to use artifact bindings which block charm use and essence regeneration and after a certain point you can't say those are standard issue to all of Creations jails with a straight face. So there are just some types of games that you can only really play in the Exalted setting by using terrestrials.<br /> <br /> <b>2. You Want a Challenge:</b><br /> It is inevitable that groups swap out players, old ones get different job hours or classes, so you bring in some new blood and teach them the game system. I find it works well to have the experienced players run Terrestrial characters and let the new players run celestial exalts. This gives the experienced players a change of pace, a bit of a challenge, and it forces them to use setting knowledge rather than say power level knowledge. With the new players the power level of their charms allows them to contribute to the game without needing to know much about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Admittedly this requires an ST who can work with these concepts to pull it off in a satisfying way. Such as keeping in mind that Terrestrials are the ones who can use their charms publically without getting a Wyld Hunt called on them.<br /> <br /> Personally I had a lot of fun being the only Terrestrial in a mix group of Celestials because the character could be the public face of the group which allows for lots of role play and quick thinking moments. Sure you can't go toe to toe with the heavy hitters of the setting, but that never really bothered me. Terrestrials really should be played a lot like Xanatos from the Gargoyles series. He is much weaker than the Gargoyles, he heals much slower, he can't fly on his own, and he isn't that physically durable. But by using his wits and resources to their fullest, he can be the equal of the Gargoyles.<br /> <br /> Then again a lot of players out there just don't have the interest in that kind of play style, they just want an &quot;I win button&quot; character build where you take a specific set of charms and turn their brains off since acting like a murder-hobo is their apex of fun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T12:55:10-08:00","id":327334,"title":"","content":"If you're going concept =&gt; exalt type =&gt; character then don't bother. You might come up with a sidereal or a lunar, but you're really not going to come up with a DB. With DB chargen you start by deciding what aspect of DB you are and how you can cram your concept into its elemental themes. In second edition, unlike Solars, they had low enough power to meaningfully interact with some big parts of the setting that Solars couldn't. <br /> <br /> I've got a question for you though, why do you want to like DBs?<br /> <br /> Oh also Mnemon would school Arianna in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T13:36:35-08:00","id":327356,"title":"","content":"I think this comic perfectly illustrates converse. Why would you ever want to play a solar in 2nd edition ? In the comic above, you have Princess Mnemoe with backstory, personality and a point to make. She's got power, position and a silly purpose. In comes mr solar jerkbag who emulates what solars do best: Trolls waggling blanket/keyword immunity and demonstrating what's least fun about the system. He has no story, no place in the world and no friends; just an abundance of entitlement.<br /> <br /> My 2 dinar? I'd happily play Princess Mnemoe any day and leave Solar McTrollFace to go polish his golden totem to show off to others who want to bask in its overhyped shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T14:17:11-08:00","id":327364,"title":"","content":"It all depends on what character concept you want to play. Dragon blooded powers aren't flashy, but they have a unique place in society. I like Dragon Blooded because they have investment and ties to the world. Heck, the Solar I am currently playing is from a Dragon blooded background. She had no interest in tearing the current DB governments and institutions down. Maybe bring the standard of living up to a First Age Level, but all that running society stuff sounds boring and time consuming. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T14:46:17-08:00","id":327402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327222#post327222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, that's a thought. Would it be game breaking to give dragonbloods an PPE-style charm that lets them learn appropriate-aspect elemental charms as if they were an Eclipse? Or is that already a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a more interesting idea than my own. DotFA has an Essence 6 Lore Charm that allows for a DB to bond spiritually with an element of their own nature and this gives them access to all of their Spirit Charms. Why not simplify things and just house-rule it that DBs can learn Elemental Spirit Charms? I like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T14:46:58-08:00","id":327404,"title":"","content":"Power level aside, I like the flavor of a lot of their charms and martial arts. I looked at their bureaucracy tree and then explained it to a friend playing a Solar bureaucrat, needless to say he was rather surprised by how much of the Dragon-Blooded charms stood out from the Solar ones. The ability to conceal fine print within agreements, detect the perfect bribe, and detect the max/min price someone is willing to take in a deal are all very cool and further lend DBs a hand when it comes to games involving working in and around organizations. Then there's White Veil Style and Even Blade style which have amazing stories and implications, from the fluff at least.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I would also like the emphasis on how weak they are toned way the fuck down for 3E. I mean come on, we can't even credit them for creating terrestrial martial arts? (as written in 2E anyways)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T14:58:11-08:00","id":327407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifnir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327404#post327404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Admittedly, I would also like the emphasis on how weak they are toned way the fuck down for 3E. I mean come on, we can't even credit them for creating terrestrial martial arts? (as written in 2E anyways)</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Since when has this ever been a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T15:04:00-08:00","id":327409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quoting this next time people complain about the Reclamation</div> </div> </div> </div> The Guild, the Threshold and the Solars are not written around their forceful intrusion into all other concerns, nor would it matter if they did because the scale of their consequences is not big enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T15:06:02-08:00","id":327412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327407#post327407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? Since when has this ever been a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>2E put forward that the Sidereals created the Immaculate Dragon Styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T15:08:43-08:00","id":327414,"title":"","content":"What I like about Dragon-Blooded is their place in the setting as decadent warrior aristocrats who have managed to hold the world together without being more dangerous to it than the enemies of Creation. I think Sidereals are agents of heaven, Lunars and Solars can be queens, but only Dragon-Blooded are actual nobility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T15:10:58-08:00","id":327416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327412#post327412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2E put forward that the Sidereals created the Immaculate Dragon Styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, well those are CMA. Even learning them is stretching the limits of a terrestrials soul, I'm okay with them not developing them from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T15:46:51-08:00","id":327438,"title":"","content":"I'm currently playing a Heptagram game, which is to say &quot;Hogwarts meets Exalted,&quot; and I've been having a lot of fun playing the religious boy who discovers that most of his texts are written by Anathema, angsted really hard, and sacrificed an enormous amount for his initiation into sorcery because he wants power to discover The Truth.<br /> <br /> In addition, the monologue I gave for stunting a binding roll against a teodozjia would have been impossible to give as any other Exalt type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T16:23:08-08:00","id":327451,"title":"","content":"There are certain themes you can do with DBs that don't really work well for anyone else. Academy (e.g. high school) games, games involving everyone being members of the same family or military unit, the experience of being an occupying power in a foreign land, high level politicking with supernatural entities. And while any Exalted can be entitled jerks, DBs have the social sanction for it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327416#post327416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, well those are CMA. Even learning them is stretching the limits of a terrestrials soul, I'm okay with them not developing them from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the TMA/CMA delineations are largely going the way of the dodo for 3e, I see no reason not to give DBs a little bit more agency in creating their own high-power fighting styles versus making them even more Sidereal sock puppets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327154#post327154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quoting this next time people complain about the Reclamation...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>DBs being Wyld Hunters fighting Solars is not the default plot of DB games, unlike the Reclamation being the default plot of Infernals games. So there is a difference. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T18:31:11-08:00","id":327538,"title":"","content":"Uhhm.... Because they're Awesome? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Considering you mention pre-errata, I get the feeling that yor're coming from a 2ed-based perspective. Maybe that has something to do with it?<br /> I had always only played first edition, until I decided to try out second for a new campaign last year. I.hate.2ed. for many (many (many)) reasons, but that is just digression. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (I guess my point is; &quot;don't listen to anything 2ed&quot; says, and &quot;1ed was really good&quot;)<br /> <br /> DBs are definately my favorite exalted type. This comes from several points two of which I will write about in short, but hopefully engulfing, sumaries here:<br /> <br /> <b>They have the most interesting culture</b> (<i>or: Crouching Vampire, Hidden Thrones</i>)<br /> As opposed to Solars, which are usually by default wanderers or outcasts, the Dragon-Blooded actually have a rich cultural background and heritage. Their society is probably the one with the largest page count owing to it being described in quite some detail in both the core book (1ed) and their own book (Exalted: The DragonbBlooded(1st ed.)), and hence the one with the most depth to it in the setting. The fact that it takes up so large a space in the [1ed] Rule Book, says something about how important and influential it actually is on the setting. The large presence of The Realm, and the way a Dragon-Blooded character is necessarily tied to, or a part of, creates a type of story not found in any of the other types. A DB game is not a super hero game, but an exploration of the rather complex themes embodied in the Scarlet Dynasty.<br /> <b><i>Short Version:</i></b> Dragon-Blooded is more akin to playing Vampire: The Masquerade; the point and the focus is not on being a powerful entity, the focus is more on the political side of things. The point is about being a part of a society of those powerful entities and trying to both advance (if the character is into that sort of thing) and survive in it (all this while it is being confronted by threats, both from the outside and internally).<br /> <br /> <b>Interesting Characters</b> (<i>or: how I learned to stop worrying and love the Scarlet Empress</i>)<br /> The nature of Dragon-Blooded society is ripe with interesting conflicts, difficult questions of morality, contradictions and double standards (themes such as Imperialism, control vs. freedom, truth vs. good, love vs. responsibility, a whole bunch of questions about family relations, etc. etc. not to mention all the political intrigue that comes with just belonging to a house.) The many layers of conflict and interesting social issues that one needs to take into account, when creating a character from the Scarlet Dynasty, basically makes you (that's &quot;makes&quot; as in &quot;forces&quot;) end up with a complex character. The book basically gives you a complex background for your character to relate to, and by defining hirs relation to that complex background the character will unavoidably be shaped by it.<br /> <b><i>Short Version:</i></b> The Scarlet Dynasty is a complex multilayered society. The Scarlet Dynasty is a big part of your character = you character is by default a a complex, (probably interesting) character.<br /> <br /> I could go on, but I have taken far too long to write this post as it is (which probably isn't as beutifully written as I would've liked anyway because of how late it is).<br /> Well, Hope I may have conveyed something of interest at least. Now Gooo*yawn*od night!<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T19:15:36-08:00","id":327572,"title":"","content":"I have to say, even in 1e when it worked, the DB charmset was not very exciting. DBs were always awesome, but I look forward to their charms being done by people who are excited about how cool DBs are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T19:18:22-08:00","id":327573,"title":"","content":"To be a Dragonblood to me, is to be a masterful showperson in addition to being an Exalt. To be part of the Ten Thousand is to move amongst your peers and influence them with both force and threats therein. That's part of their appeal to me, that courtly intrigue is not only a feature, it's largely expected, as your ancestry, your ancestry's baggage and all that that entails figures both into your ambitions, but also your obligations. This is some rich stuff, and while the Celestials can indeed do this, they lack the community focus that Dragonbloods have, working and figuring as an individual, not as a member of a family or a lineage. <br /> <br /> This is of course, a vanilla description, and I have seen Solars from threshold nations who were obsessed with their clan and lineage, but that's just how I perceive them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T19:48:48-08:00","id":327585,"title":"","content":"This may seem strange but, really, the only things that keep me from wanting to play the Dragon-Blooded are:<br /> <br /> 1. Their naming conventions. I find their family and given names difficult to pronounce. Even when I'm pronouncing them correctly, they don't sound right to me, and for someone who loves names and languages, this is a weird problem for me to have.<br /> <br /> 2. The aforementioned inability to manipulate their own element; which isn't a problem when I house-rule that they have certain Spirit Charms naturally, but it's still weird that the devs are actively against this idea. I have never understood their reasoning behind it and, everytime it's explained it just seems like a thinly-veiled cop-out. As though they're saying, &quot;We don't want them to have this ability, and we don't have a good reason why. It's just not going to happen and here's a non-sense pseudo-reason for it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T20:34:09-08:00","id":327632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've got a question for you though, why do you want to like DBs? </div> </div> </div>They are the most numerous Exalted in Creation so I figure that I should at least like them a bit to include them in my game or else it gonna look so weird going on adventure and never met a single DB. So basically, that nagging feeling that you left out one of the original five splat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh also Mnemon would school Arianna in a fight. </div> </div> </div>Weeellll, one of the supplement give Arianna Essence 5 and Solar Circle Sorcery.....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm going to quote the best bit of advice ever given about Dragon-Blooded games because I think it can be extrapolated to some of the best advice about Exalted in general. </div> </div> </div>Don't include what you don't like in your game, huh, simple but quite effective advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T20:49:53-08:00","id":327651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327632#post327632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weeellll, one of the supplement give Arianna Essence 5 and Solar Circle Sorcery.....</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is Mnemon's Terrestrial Martial Art training that is being referred to, as sorcery is generally an awful approach to actual fights (abrupt murder being in a different category in my mind)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327407#post327407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What? Since when has this ever been a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this was published. I find it a classic example of an inappropriately placed insult to Dragon-Blooded potential when they can't even be cool within their own splat book.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manual of Exalted Power Dragon-Blooded page 189</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">TERRESTRIAL STYLES<br /> Created for use of the weaker Terrestrial Exalted by their<br /> more powerful Celestial companions...</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T20:53:00-08:00","id":327655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifnir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327651#post327651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this was published. I find it a classic example of an inappropriately placed insult to Dragon-Blooded potential when they can't even be cool within their own splat book.</div> </div> </div> </div>MoEP: DB is full of this kind of thing. It's amazing. It's a book purely about the Dragon-Blooded and yet it looks like it's been written by someone who absolutely loathes the Dragon-Blooded and sneaks in insults at every opportunity, or like a pick-up artist negging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T20:55:43-08:00","id":327660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327632#post327632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weeellll, one of the supplement give Arianna Essence 5 and Solar Circle Sorcery.....</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sorcery looks impressive but is actually pretty shit in 2e rules, the high Essence just lets you spam perfects. Yawn. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327632#post327632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't include what you don't like in your game, huh, simple but quite effective advice.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a bad notion to follow, however, there's only so much that can be done when a splat hyper focuses on a particular kind of game and no support is ever offered for any other kind of game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T20:58:09-08:00","id":327661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327655#post327655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MoEP: DB is full of this kind of thing. It's amazing. It's a book purely about the Dragon-Blooded and yet it looks like it's been written by someone who absolutely loathes the Dragon-Blooded and sneaks in insults at every opportunity, or like a pick-up artist negging.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I hope they will cut the needless, and seemingly spiteful, reminders of power tiers in the 3E splat books. Each splat needs the chance to be awesome and playable and not ruined by the text constantly reminding the reader of how fucked a player might be for not deciding to play something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T21:29:56-08:00","id":327682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifnir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327661#post327661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I hope they will cut the needless, and seemingly spiteful, reminders of power tiers in the 3E splat books. Each splat needs the chance to be awesome and playable and not ruined by the text constantly reminding the reader of how fucked a player might be for not deciding to play something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that...could get excessive. Like that sidebar saying how DBs are viewed as being dirtier than street urchins in Heaven, because even a beggar could become a Solar, but the Scarlet Empress never could. <br /> <br /> if you're playing a DB you'll get reminded of how low you are whenever your whole circle gets schooled by a Solar who didn't even burn peripheral. You don't really need to have the salt god who you're trying to make diplomacy with respect Foul Ol Ron more than you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T22:18:43-08:00","id":327718,"title":"","content":"You're missing the final panel with Mnemoe looking dejected and going Mnyoro~n","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T22:27:11-08:00","id":327719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kawaiiwolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327356#post327356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this comic perfectly illustrates converse. Why would you ever want to play a solar in 2nd edition ? In the comic above, you have Princess Mnemoe with backstory, personality and a point to make. She's got power, position and a silly purpose. In comes mr solar jerkbag who emulates what solars do best: Trolls waggling blanket/keyword immunity and demonstrating what's least fun about the system. He has no story, no place in the world and no friends; just an abundance of entitlement.<br /> <br /> My 2 dinar? I'd happily play Princess Mnemoe any day and leave Solar McTrollFace to go polish his golden totem to show off to others who want to bask in its overhyped shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you seriously arguing a conclusion from that comic? As much as I like Jen's stuff (at one point, conversation here got so low-key, that I was practically &quot;just here for the Jen-comi!&quot;), it's pretty clear there's a strong bias there. Not to mention that he's just being goofy (although I would like to see Mnemoe's face if one of her cow targets was really a Lunar!)...<br /> <br /> Leaving aside the comic, who says that Solars by default have &quot;no story&quot; or place or friends? If that's ever true at anyone's table that's the fault of the players for making bland PCs, and of the ST for not demanding better. Are Outcaste DBs equally devoid of position and purpose in the world, just because they don't belong to the Scarlet Dynasty? If so, then this is a &quot;problem&quot; that goes well beyond Solars; if not, then Solars can have life breathed into them just as well as unconnected Outcastes can!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T22:32:37-08:00","id":327721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327632#post327632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are the most numerous Exalted in Creation so I figure that I should at least like them a bit to include them in my game or else it gonna look so weird going on adventure and never met a single DB. So basically, that nagging feeling that you left out one of the original five splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you don't. If you don't like them, and don't &quot;get&quot; them to the point that you can't do them justice, then just don't use them. <br /> <br /> I believe that Creation is so large, that even with more than 10K Terrestrials around, you can statistically justify your players just never running across any. Personally, I think most people in the Realm probably rarely actually see one, and when they do, the Dynast is just out shopping, or overseeing workers, or the like. Probably only the soldiers in the Legions ever actually get to see them in action, charms blazing and all...And then they go home and spread the stories to their friends and families.<br /> <br /> But in the Threshold, sightings are even rarer, I'm sure.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T22:39:35-08:00","id":327738,"title":"","content":"Another thing is that I don't like about them is lots of their charms feel like it could be port to the Solar charmset and people who are new to the game won't even notice the difference.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm such an awesome musician that I can kill people with my instrument&quot; or &quot;I'm such an awesome archer that I can parry arrow with my arrow !&quot; are some example, the only part that feel distinct are the one that focus on the &quot;Elemental Aristocrat&quot; theme like their Socialize tree or the Shout charm-cascade of Presence which are just hot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327718#post327718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing the final panel with Mnemoe looking dejected and going Mnyoro~n</div> </div> </div> </div>But that panel will be so alone without any of its friend standing next to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T22:40:06-08:00","id":327755,"title":"","content":"I don't see the books continually mentioning how DBs are &quot;weaker&quot; than Celestials as &quot;insulting&quot; at all. It's just a statement of fact, not a statement of relative value (unless the game or the reader directly correlates &quot;Power&quot; with &quot;Personal Value&quot;). <br /> <br /> In fact, as I recall, a little while ago, everyone was in an uproar because MoEP: DB praised players for choosing to play Terrestrials because choosing to play weaker PCs probably meant that they were NOT Power Gamers, or words to the effect!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've always liked the notion that while DBs were hot shit on Earth, in Heaven they were little better than jumped up pets. I never saw this as insulting the splat as a whole, but showing how relative their position and power in the world really was, and how shocking each individual Dynast, utterly convinced that the world revolves around their kind, would take this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T22:44:24-08:00","id":327798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327719#post327719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you seriously arguing a conclusion from that comic? As much as I like Jen's stuff (at one point, conversation here got so low-key, that I was practically &quot;just here for the Jen-comi!&quot;), it's pretty clear there's a strong bias there. Not to mention that he's just being goofy (although I would like to see Mnemoe's face if one of her cow targets was really a Lunar!)...</div> </div> </div> </div>Killing cows has been a proud tradition of Exalted ever since the dawn of time (Hinduism are about to ceremoniously slay thousand of cow in Indian/Nepal as we speak) ! I'm sure there are some heaven law that prevent Lunar from ruining everyone cow-killing fun with their shape-shifting....<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://th00.deviantart.net/fs19/PRE/f/2007/293/5/7/Sidereals__You__ve_got_mail_by_PaleLonginus.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 12-02-2014, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T23:01:20-08:00","id":327900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327738#post327738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing is that I don't like about them is lots of their charms feel like it could be port to the Solar charmset and people who are new to the game won't even notice the difference.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;I'm such an awesome musician that I can kill people with my instrument&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;I'm such an awesome archer that I can parry arrow with my arrow !&amp;quot; are some example, the only part that feel distinct are the one that focus on the &amp;quot;Elemental Aristocrat&amp;quot; theme like their Socialize tree or the Shout charm-cascade of Presence which are just hot.</div> </div> </div> </div>THIS has really started to bug me recently actually. Dragonfly Finds Mate is such a solar charm that it hurts, and so are at least a dozen other DB charms. I really hope DFM is in the codebook for Solars and replaced by something else. It would be like if DBs randomly had a charm to track a target by following their strand of fate, it just doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327755#post327755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the books continually mentioning how DBs are &amp;quot;weaker&amp;quot; than Celestials as &amp;quot;insulting&amp;quot; at all. It's just a statement of fact, not a statement of relative value (unless the game or the reader directly correlates &amp;quot;Power&amp;quot; with &amp;quot;Personal Value&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. <br /> <br /> In fact, as I recall, a little while ago, everyone was in an uproar because MoEP: DB praised players for choosing to play Terrestrials because choosing to play weaker PCs probably meant that they were NOT Power Gamers, or words to the effect!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've always liked the notion that while DBs were hot shit on Earth, in Heaven they were little better than jumped up pets. I never saw this as insulting the splat as a whole, but showing how relative their position and power in the world really was, and how shocking each individual Dynast, utterly convinced that the world revolves around their kind, would take this!</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue isn't necessairily that DBs are legally property not persons in Heaven, my issue is that a god would rather treat with an illiterate, rapist thief than the woman who fired the Sword of Creation and saved the world. After all he might be slitting the throat of his latest victim while scratching his STD sores, but she doesn't even have a chance of becoming one of the celestial exalted. Hate her? Sure! Disrespect her? How could you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T23:45:59-08:00","id":327949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327755#post327755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the books continually mentioning how DBs are &quot;weaker&quot; than Celestials as &quot;insulting&quot; at all. It's just a statement of fact, not a statement of relative value (unless the game or the reader directly correlates &quot;Power&quot; with &quot;Personal Value&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>The gameline has done quite a lot of &quot;only the Solar Exalted could possibly deal with Important Problem X&quot; (EDIT: and more importantly, doesn't say this about any other kind of Exalt), and the devs have talked about how &quot;Creation <i>needs</i> the Solars&quot;. These kinds of statements might not <i>say</i> that your personal value is a function of what type of Exalt you are, but they certainly glance furtively in that direction while winking at the reader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","user":"Couch","date":". 12-02-2014, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T23:52:48-08:00","id":327951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327655#post327655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MoEP: DB is full of this kind of thing. It's amazing. It's a book purely about the Dragon-Blooded and yet it looks like it's been written by someone who absolutely loathes the Dragon-Blooded and sneaks in insults at every opportunity, or like a pick-up artist negging.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, 2e hated all non-Solar and non-Infernal Exalts with a burning passion. It's not really a thing that was exclusive to Dragon-Blooded...pretty much every MoEP was dripping with contempt for their subject Exalts. Though I do admit that the shot at Dragon-Blooded in Compass: Yu-Shan was pretty blatant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T00:26:35-08:00","id":327962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327655#post327655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MoEP: DB is full of this kind of thing. It's amazing. It's a book purely about the Dragon-Blooded and yet it looks like it's been written by someone who absolutely loathes the Dragon-Blooded and sneaks in insults at every opportunity, or like a pick-up artist negging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ayup. I despise most of MoEP: DBs for this reason. The book should feel like a demonstration of how cool and interesting the DBs are, but instead it's written purely to show off how useless and pitiful they are in comparison to the all-powerful Solars. Stuff like the descriptions of their perfect defences - &quot;this is a shitty charm that nobody should ever use, but the DBs are so pathetic that they have no other options&quot; is not the kind of thing I want to read while picking out charms for my character. It should be &quot;these are the mighty Exalted and this is how super-awesome they are, even if there are even more awesome people out there&quot; not &quot;why are you even reading this book, go play a Solar you dimwit&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T00:51:05-08:00","id":327967,"title":"","content":"Now there is a lot to like about the dragon-blooded they allow stories of a scope just above the mortal to practically any problem with Essence and numbers. This also make them much easier for a GM to handle since most things challanging a human scaled up to 11 will work as a credible threat/challange to DB's where a solar need a supernatural challange at every corner to even notice it is there. They are more likely to actually do things that look like co-operation in combat as they are not as powerful and have more options to do so then solars and other exalts, who usually go at things alone or in small groups because it works. It is a lot easier to integrate them into a context as they are the only splat with an actual connection to the world that isn't 100% in the hands of the GM and player. Also anyone who looks at the Exalting will see that any splat is a wonderful antagonist splat but only the DB's are really an underdog allowing for a lot of room for being the heroes in a action/horror/thriller movie like story with Celestial antagonists.<br /> <br /> Now most of this is accompained by horrible charms that need a complete rework to actually be much fun or even thematically anything but a weak version of solars. In my last solar campaign using 2E rules the players where much more concerned being boxed in by multiple anima effects then actual attacks by DB's at least initially. I would not have been running a DB game as I am currently without rewriting the charms more or less entirely and introducing alternative paths to power.<br /> <br /> What the new DB book really needs is a good example of a few hundred DB's coming together with a couple of tens of thousands of mortal followers and stomping hard on something that is percieved as really dangerous, a deathlord or something and then for the book to allow that to happen mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3085-chance","user":"chance","date":". 12-02-2014, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3085-chance","name":"chance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T03:26:26-08:00","id":328014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327951#post327951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, 2e hated all non-Solar and non-Infernal Exalts with a burning passion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it crass to make a post solely about what a ridiculous thing this is to say, even for Coik?<br /> <br /> Oh darn, it seems to have happened anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Perhaps I can salvage it.<br /> <br /> Errrmmm...<br /> <br /> I've often gotten a kick out of interpreting their social Charms in terms of the jibes of a dysfunctional family, so that appears to be one angle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The aforementioned inability to manipulate their own element</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, if Charms are being expanded into multiple elements, then there will probably be things like Craft Charms to affect things other than earth so... maybe that will scratch some of the itch? Perhaps also Brawl Charms themed around something other than water?<br /> <br /> I keep wondering what &quot;manipulate your own element&quot; is actually supposed to mean. I suppose the reference to Spirit Charms is a bit of a start, but... is Affinity Element Control actually much use? I mean as it's written; it comes across to me to be about as vague as, say, the Movement rules are, especially in terms of the rather nonsensical way it quantifies how much of a given element you can control. The only interesting description of it I ever saw was in Sikunare's Charm description in the Second Edition core, and even that seems as though it would have been more suitable as a Charm distinct to herself.<br /> <br /> But as a thing for Exalted to do? It doesn't really fit into the stylistic or mechanical conceits at all.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T04:58:19-08:00","id":328053,"title":"","content":"Affinity (Element) Control was useful in the context of a generalised spirit charmset.<br /> You could apply appropriate limitations to it based on the natural habitat or a particular elemental or classify weird things as elements allowing you to have a demon that fights people with constructs of shadow.<br /> It'd be terrible as a Dragon-Blooded charm because it'd be a one stop &quot;elemental mastery&quot; that a lot of players would feel obligated to buy despite the fact many of its actual effects are nothing new for them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 12-02-2014, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T04:59:56-08:00","id":328054,"title":"","content":"I really don't get why everyone complains about other exalted getting charms that seem to fit solar themes. Solar themes practically begin and end at &quot;being really good at shit&quot;. That's a pretty necessary component of <i>any</i> exalted splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T06:05:25-08:00","id":328120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327900#post327900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue isn't necessairily that DBs are legally property not persons in Heaven, my issue is that a god would rather treat with an illiterate, rapist thief than the woman who fired the Sword of Creation and saved the world. After all he might be slitting the throat of his latest victim while scratching his STD sores, but she doesn't even have a chance of becoming one of the celestial exalted. Hate her? Sure! Disrespect her? How could you?</div> </div> </div> </div>The impression it gave me was that the god isn't really capable of respecting the Solars either, it's just that the Mandate of Heaven is a software patch that imposes it on them.<br /> <br /> I look forward to being able to pretend it never happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T06:33:38-08:00","id":328152,"title":"","content":"That line is clearly bullshit anyway, as no other book demonstrates the celestial gods giving the barest whiff of a flying fuck about mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T06:38:52-08:00","id":328157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327721#post327721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you don't. If you don't like them, and don't &quot;get&quot; them to the point that you can't do them justice, then just don't use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Lunars, for instance!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T06:40:25-08:00","id":328158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328152#post328152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That line is clearly bullshit anyway, as no other book demonstrates the celestial gods giving the barest whiff of a flying fuck about mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but it's a really easy spot to point out where they crossed the line from &quot;you're the weakest of the exalted, the least heroes, now what are you going to do about it?&quot; to &quot; hey guess what, no matter who you are or what you've done any mortal commands more dignity and respect in heaven because your sould has been tainted by the weak, cowardly, treacherous blood of dragons.&quot;.<br /> <br /> But the codebook is almost out so its time to get hyped for Solars anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T07:00:01-08:00","id":328173,"title":"","content":"You could put a positive spin on it and say what the book actually meant is that dragonbloods don't <i>automatically</i> get respect for being a dragonblooded the same way that a solar gets respect for being a solar. On an individual basis, yeah, you can earn props but because dragonbloods don't need to earn their exaltation in quite the same way solars do it doesn't carry the same weight on its own in the eyes of the gods.<br /> <br /> Also the gods have always been a bit racist towards elementally-aspected beings to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T07:02:23-08:00","id":328174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327738#post327738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing is that I don't like about them is lots of their charms feel like it could be port to the Solar charmset and people who are new to the game won't even notice the difference.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm such an awesome musician that I can kill people with my instrument&quot; or &quot;I'm such an awesome archer that I can parry arrow with my arrow !&quot; are some example, the only part that feel distinct are the one that focus on the &quot;Elemental Aristocrat&quot; theme like their Socialize tree or the Shout charm-cascade of Presence which are just hot.</div> </div> </div> </div>(1) Every Exalt is going to have some &quot;Solar kinda stuff&quot; in their Charmset, because &quot;Solar kinda stuff&quot; basically means &quot;I'm good at This Thing&quot; and every splat needs something like that.<br /> (2) Those specific things you mention? Go take a look at Legends of the Wulin. It's no coincidence that Jenna Moran was involved in both. You see some classic DB elemental powers in the Elemental Internal Styles and some things like the classic &quot;I fight with the music I make&quot; in a Formless technique. Of course, these are definitely tropes from wuxia and Eastern legend, and DBs fall into that thematic much more as a default, being soldiers and bureaucrats of a government headed by a divine or semi-divine figure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T07:52:12-08:00","id":328204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (1) Every Exalt is going to have some &quot;Solar kinda stuff&quot; in their Charmset, because &quot;Solar kinda stuff&quot; basically means &quot;I'm good at This Thing&quot; and every splat needs something like that. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, I don't think this quite true regarding those charms that I mention. Take Forgotten Earth from Sid Athletic for example, it's basically just a jump-enhancer like Monkey Leap Technique, but the charm fluff, instead of &quot;Sidereal are so awesome they can jump very high&quot;, it's &quot;Sidereal can jump so high because they cut the distance between them and the ground&quot;.<br /> <br /> But Dragonfly Finds Mate are not like that, parrying arrow using your arrow is very Solar, and the charm fluff take don't make any effort trying to make the charm feel distinctive, like the Wood Aspect actually make the their arrow have a crush to the enemy arrow, it's instead &quot;DB are so awesome they can defend again attack using arrow&quot;. And Ex2 DB has lots of charms like that, which is probably why some people want them to have more bending charms me think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (2) Those specific things you mention? Go take a look at Legends of the Wulin. It's no coincidence that Jenna Moran was involved in both. You see some classic DB elemental powers in the Elemental Internal Styles and some things like the classic &quot;I fight with the music I make&quot; in a Formless technique. Of course, these are definitely tropes from wuxia and Eastern legend, and DBs fall into that thematic much more as a default, being soldiers and bureaucrats of a government headed by a divine or semi-divine figure. </div> </div> </div>Eh, this is the first time I have heard DB being more wuxia than Solar. And I don't see &quot;soldiers and bureaucrats of a government headed by a divine or semi-divine figure&quot; having any connection to wuxia at all, most main characters in wuxia stories are wanderer or student of various martial art sect instead of soldier or bureaucrats, it sound more like Solar to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 12-02-2014, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T07:53:53-08:00","id":328205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328014#post328014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it crass to make a post solely about what a ridiculous thing this is to say, even for Coik?<br /> <br /> Oh darn, it seems to have happened anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Perhaps I can salvage it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars and Infernals both got multiple books with quality mechanics, and in the case of Infernals, the &quot;big thing&quot; for the edition, Devil Tigers. The Reclamation is presented as <i>the thing happening right now</i> in the setting, even getting a huge adventure book devoted to it, even if it was shite. Solars get things like cap bursters that let them play with toys that legitimately should be beyond the reach of any &quot;normal&quot; campaign because, well, what's the point of writing a hundred high Essence Charms for them if no one gets to use them?<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded got shit mechanics, including the &quot;fails against magic&quot; clause, which is so nebulous as to make a lot of their Charms potentially useless depending on how you interpret it. They are disrespected in almost every mention, including the line about how gods view them as less than mortals, because at least mortals can get a &quot;real&quot; Exaltation. The Realm is also presented as a complete, toothless joke that any Solar should be able to conquer on a lazy Saturday when they're not feeling particularly ambitious.<br /> <br /> Sidereals got absolutely catastrophic mechanics, basically a slapdash copy-paste from 1e that did nothing to adjust them to fit new mechanical conceits within the edition. The Bureau of Destinty is presented as completely incompotent, which then makes sense when they're casually wiped out in the aforementioned shite adventure because the writers clearly couldn't or were too lazy to account for their impact on the adventure as written. Garbage like Sidereals being executed by Heaven for anything short of high treason also makes its way into the setting.<br /> <br /> Lunars get shit mechanics, but in contrast to Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals are let off easy setting-wise because other than Thousand Streams River, they're pretty much completely ignored.<br /> <br /> Abyssals get shit mechanics (notice a pattern here?) and basically shoehorned into &quot;Deathlord's bitch&quot; or &quot;Redemption&quot; arcs.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Isator, you are correct. I don't see why I should think that the only two splats who got polished mechanics, continuing support throughout the edition, and weren't made into mooks were the favored sons of the edition. Admittingly things got a bit better with Glories and 2.5, but that's kinda like me releasing a comprehensive balance patch for my MMO a week before I turn the servers off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T08:04:25-08:00","id":328213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328205#post328205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm is also presented as a complete, toothless joke that any Solar should be able to conquer on a lazy Saturday when they're not feeling particularly ambitious.</div> </div> </div> </div>All right, Coik, challenge accepted. Put your money where your mouth is. Contact me on Skype, we'll roll this shit out. You'll play a Solar that I give you (&quot;any Solar,&quot; you said), and I'll play the Realm. You have one day to completely conquer me.<br /> <br /> For the sake of fairness, I'm even going to forego giving you a guy with all Ox-Bodies and the like, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-02-2014, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T08:06:52-08:00","id":328217,"title":"","content":"Also. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327220#post327220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it looks like I'll have to continue my tradition of giving DB players the <i>Affinity (Element) Control</i> Spirit Charm, then. Having elementally-empowered heroes who cannot manipulate their own element will always seem backwards and weird to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The person with elemental powers (<b>especially fire</b>) who isn't totally in control of them is iconic and not something that should be a non-issue for all Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T08:15:43-08:00","id":328225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328213#post328213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All right, Coik, challenge accepted. Put your money where your mouth is. Contact me on Skype, we'll roll this shit out. You'll play a Solar that I give you (&quot;any Solar,&quot; you said), and I'll play the Realm. You have one day to completely conquer me.<br /> <br /> For the sake of fairness, I'm even going to forego giving you a guy with all Ox-Bodies and the like, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>As potentially kinky as that sounds I think you'll be better off adding him to your ignore list. (User profile, Subscribed, Edit Settings button, Account tab scroll to the bottom and there it is.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T09:06:49-08:00","id":328274,"title":"","content":"The Sidereals would be a problem for any Solar wanting to destroy the Realm. They'd have one good surprise attack where they could wipe out the Imperial city or something but after that it's ninja assassins everywhere. I'm pretty sure even the gold faction would be against you at that point because you're really really bad for their reputation &quot;n-n-no guys really! Really they aren't all arrogant douchbags we swear! That one mass murderer is literally a crazy fluke!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T10:44:40-08:00","id":328422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328217#post328217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The person with elemental powers (<b>especially fire</b>) who isn't totally in control of them is iconic and not something that should be a non-issue for all Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I <i>want</i> characters who are totally in control of their own element (the primordial essence of which literally runs in their veins). Are the DBs supposed to be clumsy when it comes to their own Exalted legacy as the inheritors of raw elemental power?<br /> <br /> A lot of the elemental effects I wish Dragon-Blooded had could be approximated with existing Charms, but they all lack the versatility and flexibility that I deeply crave. A Fire-Elemental could start a small fire, cause the fire to leap and ignite separate candles and then dance in the air to put on a show - all with <i>one</i> Charm. A Dragon-Blooded might need two or three Charms to do the same thing. As far as I know, Earth-Aspected DBs do not have a Charm that lets them tunnel through solid earth, but an Earth Elemental could with the appropriate Charm. Does this not seem strange?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T11:00:47-08:00","id":328442,"title":"","content":"I've always kind of themed that random effects like that could be accomplished by you stunting your anima, and in fact earth aspects do have a tunnelling charm in war, it might even be the first one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T11:07:30-08:00","id":328445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328217#post328217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also. The person with elemental powers (<b>especially fire</b>) who isn't totally in control of them is iconic and not something that should be a non-issue for all Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a better theme if you're running a game of younger characters (say, in primary school) or you have Charms that cause your anima to go out of control but also give you some kind of significant advantage from it. Losing control of your fundamental magical essence seems out-of-place if you're portraying a trained, schooled expert or soldier. Maybe something like Bloodthirsty Sword-Dancer Spirit, but specific to the elemental anima? Lose a degree of control in exchange for bennies? That's a real tactical choice and should be encouraged, rather than just the stick of &quot;for some reason, only DBs have trouble with manipulating their native Essence patterns.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T11:19:36-08:00","id":328469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328445#post328445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;for some reason, only DBs have trouble with manipulating their native Essence patterns.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No this would be like asking for Solars to have a general-purpose charm to construct weapons, armour and tools from hard light because a spirit could do it.<br /> <br /> Affinity (Element) Control is like six charms from different abilities in one and only exists like that <b>because</b> it's a spirit charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 12-02-2014, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T11:37:52-08:00","id":328477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328422#post328422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this not seem strange?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. One is a being who is basically that element brought to life, the other is a human being whose prowess is interpreted through the imagery of that element.<br /> <br /> If Dragon Blooded were what you want, what would elementals be?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T11:48:50-08:00","id":328516,"title":"","content":"Since we seem to have jumped onto Anima Flux, the Elemental Dragons themselves don't seem to be in absolute control and that their relative non-involvement in Creation or Yu-Shan can most readily be attributed to them being walking natural disasters who'd sooner not be jerks about it.<br /> <br /> The control the Dragon-Blooded demonstrate via their ability based charms could be using humanity to temper primordial magnificence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 12-02-2014, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T11:56:54-08:00","id":328526,"title":"","content":"Imma plug the &quot;Why do you like Dragon blooded?&quot; thread, because I still feel it was a cool conversation on the topic that didn't get bogged down in &quot;Why do you dislike the Solars?&quot; or &quot;Why don't Dragonblooded get no respect?&quot; or anything like that - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...dragon-blooded</a> <br /> <br /> On the Dragonblooded themselves, I feel like I want to say again that, although I get why people want the Dragonblooded themselves to be able to manipulate and use the elements externally, and they should be able to do this, I do still feel like this is less cool than being able to say &quot;Be water&quot;.<br /> <br /> Being able to call up the nature of your element through yourself, into your aspect and your nature, through your great enlightenment and your great skill and become like it, and become stronger, better, purer, higher, through doing so, at practically any skill you can imagine.<br /> <br /> That's a lot of what inspires me about the Dragonblooded* and what I wouldn't want to be crowded out by external elemental manipulation. I feel like that's quite different in feel to the Solars' way of calling up their own essence or the bright essence of the Unconquered Sun within them.<br /> <br /> *Other inspirational points for the DBs with me are- <br /> <br /> Firstly me being a massive sucker for The Unchosen One trope- <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheUnchosenOne\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...TheUnchosenOne</a> . Seriously, if you want me to like the Chosen One better than the Unchosen One you need Gene Wolfe level storytelling!<br /> <br /> And secondly, me being again, a complete sucker, for cheering for quite good people struggling to rise above their background in bad societies, particularly that being a much less silly version of Melnibone sets you up to be able to play Elric, or at least more interesting versions of Cymoril or Yyrkoon (the apathetic aristocrat and the loyalist supremacist respectively).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T11:57:53-08:00","id":328527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328469#post328469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No this would be like asking for Solars to have a general-purpose charm to construct weapons, armour and tools from hard light because a spirit could do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's really that similar. Not having a Charm that you want isn't the same as having drawbacks due to your very nature. Having a lack of control of your element...well, I suppose how that is portrayed when you're talking about the iconic view...I just worry it'd look a little too much like a DB version of formlock.<br /> <br /> Maybe it'd be helpful if you described what kinds of occurrences/actions/consequences you might think to see from a DB who has lost control of his element?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T12:02:48-08:00","id":328530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328527#post328527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's really that similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>...That was the original thing that was being discussed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it'd be helpful if you described what kinds of occurrences/actions/consequences you might think to see from a DB who has lost control of his element?</div> </div> </div> </div>General Zhao. Less that he's lost control and more that he never embraced the non-destructive side of Firebending.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 12-02-2014, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T12:29:35-08:00","id":328537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328526#post328526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And secondly, me being again, a complete sucker, for cheering for quite good people struggling to rise above their background in bad societies, particularly that being a much less silly version of Melnibone sets you up to be able to play Elric, or at least more interesting versions of Cymoril or Yyrkoon (the apathetic aristocrat and the loyalist supremacist respectively).</div> </div> </div> </div>I should note that the version of Cymoril in the Ruby Throne graphic novel kind of rocks. Yyrkoon showed some signs of being a little less one-note but time will tell there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 12-02-2014, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T15:32:36-08:00","id":328691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328477#post328477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the other is a human being whose prowess is interpreted through the imagery of that element.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if it's just imagery, then the DBs feel wrong to me. They shouldn't have Animas that are the manifestations of those Anima, their Charms shouldn't have elemental effects. Their powers should simply be light-shows like that of the Celestial Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328477#post328477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Dragon Blooded were what you want, what would elementals be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spiritual manifestations of the elements who don't necessarily have to have manipulative powers over their element; they can just be elementally-themed spirits. By, really, I don't see why both Elementals and Dragon-Blooded can have Charms with similar effects. This happens all the time in Exalted. Exalts with effects that mirror the effects of Primordial Charms is the clearest example.<br /> <br /> Why have Green Sun Princes if Solars already have that Charm that lets them learn the Charms of any Primordial?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":438,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","user":"wulf","date":". 12-02-2014, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T15:42:00-08:00","id":328694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should note that the version of Cymoril in the Ruby Throne graphic novel kind of rocks.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like to think that when Michael Moorcock says that there are elements that, had he thought of them, he would have put them in the original stories himself, he's talking almost exclusively about her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T15:47:08-08:00","id":328697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328691#post328691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why have Green Sun Princes if Solars already have that Charm that lets them learn the Charms of any Primordial?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that many people feel* Solars using Yozi Charms should never have been true and who are thankful it will no longer be true in EX3, you may wish to use a different example.<br /> <br /> * Rightly, in my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T16:01:37-08:00","id":328703,"title":"","content":"Okay, I concede that I will never win this argument but I will never see the alternative point of view. I want the Exalted with the blood of elemental dragons running through their veins, the grandchildren of Gaia, to be able to manipulate the elements that are ever-present in their themes and iconography with relative ease. I'm never <i>not </i>going to want this, and I know it's never going to happen. So I will continue to house-rule this for as long as I run Exalted game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T16:19:21-08:00","id":328708,"title":"","content":"In my games stunting blurs that line hard. A water aspect leaps atop a massive water spout from her anima, fire aspects making a threatening speech cause candles to burn low and dark, earth aspects strike the ground into gravel as they attempt to trip somebody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T16:39:43-08:00","id":328764,"title":"","content":"I like that, DrLoveMonkey. I think that, as a Storyteller, I feel better if I have a better idea of just how much of an element a character could manipulate through stunting. That Spirit Charm gives me a volume to calculate and even <i>Mage: The Awakening</i> gives me specific numbers so that I have a rough idea of what a character could accomplish. It is appropriate for stunting, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T19:38:14-08:00","id":328841,"title":"","content":"I'm another member of the interact-concretely school, and, honestly, I consider the idea that it <i>is</i> somehow exclusive with abstract and internal uses to be so ludicrous it's not worthy of consideration. We know, we're constantly told, that the Elements have <i>both</i> spiritual and physical aspects to them. The idea that it's <i>wrong</i> to want access to visually cool tricks like catching a bucket on the water inside it, or animating a vine to pluck a kitten out of a branch, or shaping a fireplace's flames into a dancing doll to entertain a child... I don't understand it, and it makes me angry and offended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T19:46:04-08:00","id":328845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328841#post328841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm another member of the interact-concretely school, and, honestly, I consider the idea that it <i>is</i> somehow exclusive with abstract and internal uses to be so ludicrous it's not worthy of consideration. We know, we're constantly told, that the Elements have <i>both</i> spiritual and physical aspects to them. The idea that it's <i>wrong</i> to want access to visually cool tricks like catching a bucket on the water inside it, or animating a vine to pluck a kitten out of a branch, or shaping a fireplace's flames into a dancing doll to entertain a child... I don't understand it, and it makes me angry and offended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew I wasn't the only one on these forums who felt this way. You explained it far better than I could, too, with much more evocative examples. It seems weird to purposefully hold Dragon-Blooded back in this regard, to make them <i>lesser</i> and more <i>limited. </i>They're Exalted! Limitations should be something they scoff at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T19:56:12-08:00","id":328852,"title":"","content":"Setting aside the fact that the 2e implementation was dumb, the main thing that bothers me about Anima Flux is that fire is massively, massively worse than every other type -- like, the difference between falling off a bicycle and falling off an airplane kind of worse. Every other type of flux destroys things in its general vicinity, but the Fire Aspect anima <i>starts fires</i>, which will continue to spread and burn indefinitely, in an era when fires routinely destroy cities and fire-fighting is generally limited to &quot;intentionally destroy any building nearby&quot; It's <i>in-theme,</i> but I don't feel like Fire Aspects get enough compensation for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T20:18:49-08:00","id":328855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328845#post328845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I knew I wasn't the only one on these forums who felt this way. You explained it far better than I could, too, with much more evocative examples. It seems weird to purposefully hold Dragon-Blooded back in this regard, to make them <i>lesser</i> and more <i>limited. </i>They're Exalted! Limitations should be something they scoff at.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I kind of feel like Dragonblooded are defined by their limitations way more than other exalted. There's a bunch of stuff that they can't do, even more stuff that they can't do alone, it defines almost everything they do. They can't treat properly with spirits so their relationship with them is follow-or-fist, that kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T21:25:17-08:00","id":328877,"title":"","content":"Personally, I am in favor of more charms to use elemental things directly. However, I am not in favor of having a single one-stop-shop, free-form charm that lets you manipulate the element like some sort of [element]kinetic all by itself. DB-only elemental martial arts to cover most of the Avatar-style combat stuff, plus various native Charms with versatile but well-defined effects and limits for more general uses would be my choice. Having the full Human Torch + Pyro + Zuko powerset should be a <i>heavy </i>investment in charms, in my opinion. And, of course, by no means abandoning the current charms paradigm of filtering elemental associations through Abilities, just expanding it to also include more direct manifestations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T21:42:44-08:00","id":328885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328877#post328877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I am in favor of more charms to use elemental things directly. However, I am not in favor of having a single one-stop-shop, free-form charm that lets you manipulate the element like some sort of [element]kinetic all by itself. DB-only elemental martial arts to cover most of the Avatar-style combat stuff, plus various native Charms with versatile but well-defined effects and limits for more general uses would be my choice. Having the full Human Torch + Pyro + Zuko powerset should be a <i>heavy </i>investment in charms, in my opinion. And, of course, by no means abandoning the current charms paradigm of filtering elemental associations through Abilities, just expanding it to also include more direct manifestations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider my investment in a 'one stop shop', as you put it, to be a separate question from the one under discussion. I <i>would</i> want that, but I would want it because I think that even the 2E charmsets were sprawling and bloated and far more of a pain in the ass <i>waste of time</i> than they were worth to the <i>player</i> to learn his way around - I would want <i>every</i> charm to have the same kind of flexibility as a one-stop elemental manipulation charm.<br /> <br /> I recognize that the only way I'm going to get this is by writing it myself once the game comes out, though, so it's not the point I'm arguing here. Under the existing paradigm of breaking every single thing a player might try to do up into XP-taxed tidbits of 'mother may I, no you may not', you're correct that the kind of flexibility seen from, say, Toph, would be an entire charmtree rather than a single purchase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T22:07:44-08:00","id":328915,"title":"","content":"Well said, Valles. I mean, what are the Excellencies if not one-stop dice-adders? 2E very much had a Charm Bloat problem. It makes more sense to have more streamlined Charm design. Fewer Charms with greater flexibility and application - this means less Charms for players to have to hunt through a dozen books to find, less Charms for Storytellers to have to keep in mind the errata'd rules for, and really just more fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T22:17:03-08:00","id":328919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328877#post328877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I am in favor of more charms to use elemental things directly. However, I am not in favor of having a single one-stop-shop, free-form charm that lets you manipulate the element like some sort of [element]kinetic all by itself. DB-only elemental martial arts to cover most of the Avatar-style combat stuff, plus various native Charms with versatile but well-defined effects and limits for more general uses would be my choice. Having the full Human Torch + Pyro + Zuko powerset should be a <i>heavy </i>investment in charms, in my opinion. And, of course, by no means abandoning the current charms paradigm of filtering elemental associations through Abilities, just expanding it to also include more direct manifestations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, I have no issues with it being a big investment to do tons of fancy tricks with your element. One Charm - or even free, as an Anima power - to do some basic stuff, then a bunch more specializations.<br /> <br /> I just tend to think that &quot;skill in manipulating elemental essence&quot; should be somewhat separate from the standard Abilities. *Put it all in one place* (and make that place somewhere you'd think to look without already knowing the answer, not Athletics or Lore) so that when someone wants to make a character who is all about the bending they just flick to the relevant page and start planning.<br /> <br /> Either that or make the Ability Charms *mostly* elemental in their effects - Codex Alera furycrafting is pretty darn cool (still only up to book 2. no spoilers please), and they work on a basis of metaphorical as well as literal elemental effects... but no &quot;and I guess we just need generically magical competence here&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T01:14:47-08:00","id":328990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328841#post328841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm another member of the interact-concretely school, and, honestly, I consider the idea that it <i>is</i> somehow exclusive with abstract and internal uses to be so ludicrous it's not worthy of consideration. We know, we're constantly told, that the Elements have <i>both</i> spiritual and physical aspects to them. The idea that it's <i>wrong</i> to want access to visually cool tricks like catching a bucket on the water inside it, or animating a vine to pluck a kitten out of a branch, or shaping a fireplace's flames into a dancing doll to entertain a child... I don't understand it, and it makes me angry and offended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing nobody's actually saying that and it's entirely a question of <b>when</b> and <b>how</b> they achieve such abilities. I think Affinity (Element) Control is a bad charm that only exists like it does because elementals are.<br /> -NPCs who don't have to worry about advancement<br /> -sharing a charmset with gods and demons<br /> <br /> I get the impression Wulf just wants more dramatic licence with stunts and hasn't considered that he has, for example given <b>all</b> Water Aspects the ability to poison liquid at a touch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T01:21:10-08:00","id":328994,"title":"","content":"Eh, now that we have Exigent, I wonder if people will be satisfied playing an Exigent of [element] ?<br /> <br /> An Exigent of Fire can focus on purifying theme by have Medicine charm that purge mutation or UMI from people for example, and there is the whole Sati thing, Investigation charm that involve throwing fire into someone, if they know that they have lied or feel guilt then they got damaged by the flame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 12-03-2014, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T01:27:05-08:00","id":328995,"title":"","content":"People should go to whatever's fun, of course.<br /> <br /> The logic of Dragonblooded though, in my opinion, isn't elemental imagery or manipulation, I don't think. It's more about the element moving through you, becoming like and flowing like the element, so becoming more capable of more within an ability than normal men and women can be and so breaking the bounds of mortal skill.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded can manipulate the world and the element, just as a one piece with a skilled action where the element is flowing through them. So you're not going to get a Charm which feels like its unconnected with specific skill and where the element isn't in the Dragonblooded and making them stronger at a specific skill, even if there's no problem with them effecting the outside world as well. <br /> <br /> It's about the elements running through their veins (being *inside* them, like a spirit that's taking possession) and empowering their skill. Whatever effects you can fit within that paradigm, which capture that same feel and the Dragonblooded power level are legit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T01:35:52-08:00","id":328999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328994#post328994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, now that we have Exigent, I wonder if people will be satisfied playing an Exigent of [element] ?<br /> <br /> An Exigent of Fire can focus on purifying theme by have Medicine charm that purge mutation or UMI from people for example, and there is the whole Sati thing, Investigation charm that involve throwing fire into someone, if they know that they have lied or feel guilt then they got damaged by the flame.</div> </div> </div> </div>For one, I think a lot of the fire charms you suggest seem very suitable for the Dragon blooded, and secondly... I am not sure how you have a god of purely 'fire', that doesn't feel very mythical to me, and feels more like Nobilis.<br /> <br /> Look at the list of mythological Fire gods, most of them have more purviews than just fire. Ra has the sun, Vulcan and Hephaestus have the forge. Agni is the closest thing I can find to a pure fire-god, and he is also responsible for accepting offerings from humans, and is the messenger between gods and men.<br /> <br /> Really, an Exigent of fire can work, but he would have to be mechanically and thematically distinct from a fire-aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T01:46:58-08:00","id":329004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328999#post328999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one, I think a lot of the fire charms you suggest seem very suitable for the Dragon blooded, and secondly... I am not sure how you have a god of purely 'fire', that doesn't feel very mythical to me, and feels more like Nobilis.<br /> <br /> Look at the list of mythological Fire gods, most of them have more purviews than just fire. Ra has the sun, Vulcan and Hephaestus have the forge. Agni is the closest thing I can find to a pure fire-god, and he is also responsible for accepting offerings from humans, and is the messenger between gods and men.<br /> <br /> Really, an Exigent of fire can work, but he would have to be mechanically and thematically distinct from a fire-aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I just typed [Element] and Exigent of Fire to make it simple (Exigent of Fire, and Purifying and Innocent may step on the Abyssal's toe of having overly long name :cough<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> But yeah, if I want to play a bender and my only choice is Exigent then of course I have to expand on Exigent's patron purview since God of (only) Fire is a little narrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T02:20:43-08:00","id":329015,"title":"","content":"I mused on this a while back.<br /> <br /> The God of Fire would probably be a bureaucrat who administrates when fires are supposed to happen (or not happen, as the case may be) as part of Heaven's plan they also double as an ambassador to the courts of prominent Fire Elementals. They may recognise the value of fire and be fascinated by it in ways that make the other gods nervous but it's something other to them, a force to be directed and controlled rather than something innate to them.<br /> <br /> As such the Exalt of such a god would be all about manipulating the element but their lack of an inner flame leaves them crucially lacking a means to will it into existence. Without the correct set-up they would be much weaker than a Fire Aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T02:35:00-08:00","id":329021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">animating a vine to pluck a kitten out of a branch</div> </div> </div> </div>Survival Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">shaping a fireplace's flames into a dancing doll to entertain a child</div> </div> </div> </div>Performance Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328841#post328841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">catching a bucket on the water inside it</div> </div> </div> </div>Stunted parry, I guess? This one is kind of weird.<br /> <br /> Hey, what do people think of that time Vance mentioned the planned Archery Charm that allows you to plant your bow in the ground and have it turn into a tree, providing cover and synergizing with the Charm to let you draw arrows directly from living wood?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I should not that when I picture a Terrestrial Performance Charm to make a dancing image in flames, it's one where the Exalt does something like reach into the flame and draw their hands out with puppet strings of smoke trailing from their fingers, which they then use to &quot;assemble&quot; the puppet and then twitch and draw on to make it dance. Or possibly some kind of curious reverse shadow puppetry. Maybe even some whistling that seems to harmonize with the motions in the flame until it gets to a point of such precision that subtle nuances in the sound produce an elaborate moving shape.<br /> <br /> Hmm, looking at that, I think I have an inclination more towards folklore than The Last Airbender in terms of how I think Dragon Blooded should have their elemental expression stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 12-03-2014, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T03:52:55-08:00","id":329064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328694#post328694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like to think that when Michael Moorcock says that there are elements that, had he thought of them, he would have put them in the original stories himself, he's talking almost exclusively about her.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've considered making a Daybreak based on her.<br /> A consort/royal physician who specialises in life syphoning Medicine charms who is desperately trying to keep her gravely ill ruler alive no matter the cost and is rapidly running out of allies and places to hide the bodies.<br /> I want to do her as a PC but I'd need the right group for &quot;serial killer with good intentions&quot; to not cause a rift and a ST who can portray the love interest well enough so that her devotion has a nobility to it that's gone flying off into madness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T09:11:15-08:00","id":329277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328990#post328990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good thing nobody's actually saying that and it's entirely a question of <b>when</b> and <b>how</b> they achieve such abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Huh...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328526#post328526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Dragonblooded themselves, I feel like I want to say again that, although I get why people want the Dragonblooded themselves to be able to manipulate and use the elements externally, and they should be able to do this, I do still feel like this is less cool than being able to say &quot;Be water&quot;.<br /> <br /> Being able to call up the nature of your element through yourself, into your aspect and your nature, through your great enlightenment and your great skill and become like it, and become stronger, better, purer, higher, through doing so, at practically any skill you can imagine.<br /> <br /> That's a lot of what inspires me about the Dragonblooded* and what I wouldn't want to be crowded out by external elemental manipulation. I feel like that's quite different in feel to the Solars' way of calling up their own essence or the bright essence of the Unconquered Sun within them.</div> </div> </div> </div>...So this isn't visible on page five of my browser's view of the thread, then?<br /> <br /> If you really want I'm pretty sure I can go back to the last thread this dance happened in and find several more examples for you, too.<br /> <br /> I'd even be interested to see if I can find an example or two of someone wanting <i>only</i> physical manifestations, at the same time; I've seen that railed against, but I don't recall reading any actual posts to the effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329021#post329021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Survival Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is currently forbidden, because We Shouldn't Want Bending.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329021#post329021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Performance Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is currently forbidden, because We Shouldn't Want Bending.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329021#post329021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stunted parry, I guess? This one is kind of weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is currently especially forbidden, because We Shouldn't Want Bending and We Shouldn't Try To Be Clever. And no, there's nothing weird about it - it's taking the ability to hold a ball of water and using it to catch an already moving mass of water - that happens to have a bucket around it. It's as straightforward as they come.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329021#post329021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, looking at that, I think I have an inclination more towards folklore than The Last Airbender in terms of how I think Dragon Blooded should have their elemental expression stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any difference between the two beyond the animation style. It is, after all, still fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T09:14:05-08:00","id":329279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328173#post328173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could put a positive spin on it and say what the book actually meant is that dragonbloods don't <i>automatically</i> get respect for being a dragonblooded the same way that a solar gets respect for being a solar. On an individual basis, yeah, you can earn props but because dragonbloods don't need to earn their exaltation in quite the same way solars do it doesn't carry the same weight on its own in the eyes of the gods.<br /> <br /> Also the gods have always been a bit racist towards elementally-aspected beings to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, that's a point I hadn't considered, but it makes sense!<br /> <br /> But which exact book/passage are we talking about, here? I'd like to read what it says for myself...<br /> <br /> As I've always interpreted Heaven's attitude, Gods have even less actual regard for mortals than they do for DBs; if Terrestrials are jumped-up pets, then mortals are just pets, period. The difference is that that mortal that you once refused to let into your Celestial Taxi or Bar because you don't allow &quot;his kind&quot; in *could* well come back empowered with the power of one of the Most High...and he's gonna remember you!<br /> <br /> So, it's not so much &quot;respect&quot; as it is &quot;practical self-interest&quot;. While they know exactly where they stand with the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> As to how the Scarlet Empress would be viewed and treated were she ever to set foot in Heaven? Well, that's an interesting question, and I'd like to hear some ideas on that. Personally, I think she'd be the exception, like that racist guy in Do The Right Thing who didn't like Black people, but loved Prince and Michael Jackson because they were somehow exceptions to his perception of What Black People Are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T09:25:04-08:00","id":329285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329277#post329277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is currently especially forbidden, because We Shouldn't Want Bending and We Shouldn't Try To Be Clever. And no, there's nothing weird about it - it's taking the ability to hold a ball of water and using it to catch an already moving mass of water - that happens to have a bucket around it. It's as straightforward as they come.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's throwing a damn bucket filled with water at you, so?<br /> <br /> Some kind of magic bucket that manages to retain water while in flight, no less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is currently forbidden, because We Shouldn't Want Bending.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, the old histrionics, how I've missed them.<br /> <br /> Completely disregarding my point towards that Wood Archery Charm, I'll notice.<br /> <br /> What exactly is Bending in this context?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any difference between the two beyond the animation style. It is, after all, still fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Differences in style are everything. Differences in style are why Solar Charms are being reprioritized.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T09:31:25-08:00","id":329296,"title":"","content":"I'm currently playing a DB superhero in an E5 Modern game alongside a group of Sidereals, Lunars and Alchemicals. I think it's fair to say that she's one of the group's best fighters. <br /> <br /> They have three main weaknesses in high level combat.<br /> <br /> 1) Lack of perfect defences that can block Unblockable/Undodgeable attacks. Without assistance from other DBs using Conflaguraiton of Warding, they only have one, Dragon Vortex Attack's shield function. This makes DVA and Wrath Directing Gesture important Charms for high level combat, but luckily they are great Charms in their own right even without the PD function. <br /> <br /> 2) Lack of accuracy. Unlike most other splats, DBs generally lack means to boost their accuracy temporarily beyond their base dice pools, reduce target DVs or otherwise hit high DV targets with consistency. This can be overcome using certain CMAs but I consider that cheating.<br /> <br /> 3) Reliance on External Penalties for defence. Depending on the form of attack, a DB can have around a -5 external penalty to attacks on top of their DV. This is a solid defence, but it is vulnerable to the few Charms that negate external penalties.<br /> <br /> Other than that they have a functional combat suite and are great at assisting a group. DB Dodge especially is a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T09:40:38-08:00","id":329303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329279#post329279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But which exact book/passage are we talking about, here? I'd like to read what it says for myself...<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The offending quote lies at the bottom of the sidebar on page 33 of CoCD: Yu Shan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T09:50:56-08:00","id":329308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329277#post329277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...So this isn't visible on page five of my browser's view of the thread, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're reading it differently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really want I'm pretty sure I can go back to the last thread this dance happened in and find several more examples for you, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was obviously talking about this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T10:25:59-08:00","id":329354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329277#post329277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is currently forbidden, because We Shouldn't Want Bending.</div> </div> </div> </div>When people say We Shouldn't Want Bending, they're virtually always -- even in the example you cite -- talking about something completely different. Pretty much nobody is suggesgting that Dragon-Blooded charms should not have the capacity to manipulate the elements, in the sense you seem to be implying. You're suggesting people are saying that the mere fact that a charm involves manipulating an element -- which <i>many</i> existing DB charms do -- makes it inappropriate for DBs. If anyone is saying that, it is a bizarre niche argument. What I see a lot of is people saying that they don't want that to be the defining DB gimmick, and they don't want generalized one-size-fits-all bending as a basic DB power. That said, even if someone <i>were</i> making the argument you're implying, &quot;should Dragon-Blooded have a generalized elemental manipulation power&quot; and &quot;should Dragon-Blooded have powers that manipulate elements&quot; are two totally separate arguments that are difficult to have at the same time.<br /> <br /> A related thought: a lot of the reason so many DB charms involve conjuring, rather than manipulating, elements, is because requiring you to have the element on-hand would be a hassle, and one that disproportionately burdens specific Aspects. But I could see having charms that work <i>better</i> with a lot of base elemental material to work with, which is roughly how nWoD changeling's elemental powers function. I wonder if we'll see any of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 12-03-2014, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T10:44:56-08:00","id":329407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329277#post329277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is currently forbidden, because We Shouldn't Want Bending.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can't take you seriously anymore. That is not even <i>trying </i>to argue in good faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T22:51:32-08:00","id":329902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329285#post329285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's throwing a damn bucket filled with water at you, so?<br /> <br /> Some kind of magic bucket that manages to retain water while in flight, no less.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just that somebody dropped down a well without a rope on it - or threw at you and which has a lot of splattered droplets proceeding on about the same trajectory, as inertia dictates, for you to use. It's a Spherical Bucket Of Uniform Density anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329285#post329285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Completely disregarding my point towards that Wood Archery Charm, I'll notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I don't have enough data to say if it counts, given...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329285#post329285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is Bending in this context?</div> </div> </div> </div>The key element that defines 'Bending', here, is whether or not the elemental substance involved in a charm is <i>real</i> - whether it interacts meaningfully with the rest of the universe as though it had always been there, or if it's just a special effect. My impression of DB charms as they stand is that the latter is the case; if you toss a pebble over a plant in the desert and then nail it with a Water Elemental Bolt, the plant is not watered by the splash; it is impossible to do <i>anything</i> with your anima or your charms along those lines; you could refluff most of them with 'Solar Radiance' and get nerfed Solar charms.<br /> <br /> If you interrupt the spoiled Archery charm, do you have a healthy tree growing there, to live for the rest of its natural lifespan as such, or does it turn back into a bow no matter what you do or don't do? This will determine my reaction to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329285#post329285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Differences in style are everything. Differences in style are why Solar Charms are being reprioritized.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me rephrase, then: I do not consider the above question of 'real elements vs special effects' to be a question of style - it is very much one of substance, and it is the only one I'm <i>intending</i> to pursue in this thread; others that creep in are either known dead letters, 'insufficient data', or irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329308#post329308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we're reading it differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely plausible, especially with me bringing in baggage from previous go-rounds of the topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329308#post329308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was obviously talking about this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not find it obvious, and apologize for the confusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329354#post329354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When people say We Shouldn't Want Bending, they're virtually always -- even in the example you cite -- talking about something completely different. Pretty much nobody is suggesting that Dragon-Blooded charms should not have the capacity to manipulate the elements, in the sense you seem to be implying. You're suggesting people are saying that the mere fact that a charm involves manipulating an element -- which <i>many</i> existing DB charms do -- makes it inappropriate for DBs. If anyone is saying that, it is a bizarre niche argument. What I see a lot of is people saying that they don't want that to be the defining DB gimmick, and they don't want generalized one-size-fits-all bending as a basic DB power.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I actually think that I've covered most of my response to this between my replies to Isator and Lioness, above, save that, if I <i>am</i> misinterpreting what I'm reading so comprehensively, it represents a massive and entirely positive seachange from my takeaway of the previous discussions on this topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329354#post329354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, even if someone <i>were</i> making the argument you're implying, &quot;should Dragon-Blooded have a generalized elemental manipulation power&quot; and &quot;should Dragon-Blooded have powers that manipulate elements&quot; are two totally separate arguments that are difficult to have at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter is the discussion I'm intending to have; the former I also hold true, as part of the general position that <i>all</i> charms should be that flexible, but I recognize that it's only going to happen in a fan-rewrite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329354#post329354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A related thought: a lot of the reason so many DB charms involve conjuring, rather than manipulating, elements, is because requiring you to have the element on-hand would be a hassle, and one that disproportionately burdens specific Aspects. But I could see having charms that work <i>better</i> with a lot of base elemental material to work with, which is roughly how nWoD changeling's elemental powers function. I wonder if we'll see any of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conjuring I can live with, although I don't consider it necessary given that the anima flux <i>should</i> already do that. My concern is if they continue to evaporate away like something a computer game's stopped rendering as no longer relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329407#post329407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I can't take you seriously anymore. That is not even <i>trying </i>to argue in good faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good faith, but much emotion. That clouds the clarity of both reading and expression, no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T01:00:15-08:00","id":329937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329902#post329902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entirely plausible, especially with me bringing in baggage from previous go-rounds of the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please try not to do this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T01:05:33-08:00","id":329939,"title":"","content":"Wait, DB anima amd powers aren't real? Like I'd two wood aspects duelled for several minutes using only EBA the ground would not be littered with vines and shit? My mind is blown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T01:16:52-08:00","id":329942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329937#post329937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please try not to do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll do my best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329939#post329939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, DB anima amd powers aren't real? Like I'd two wood aspects duelled for several minutes using only EBA the ground would not be littered with vines and shit? My mind is blown.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is indeed the impression left on me by the previous editions' mechanics. I get absolutely no impression of actual <i>connection</i>, on <i>any</i> level, to the elements of the world from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","user":"Valles","date":". 12-04-2014, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T01:24:31-08:00","id":329946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328422#post328422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I <i>want</i> characters who are totally in control of their own element (the primordial essence of which literally runs in their veins). Are the DBs supposed to be clumsy when it comes to their own Exalted legacy as the inheritors of raw elemental power?<br /> <br /> A lot of the elemental effects I wish Dragon-Blooded had could be approximated with existing Charms, but they all lack the versatility and flexibility that I deeply crave. A Fire-Elemental could start a small fire, cause the fire to leap and ignite separate candles and then dance in the air to put on a show - all with <i>one</i> Charm. A Dragon-Blooded might need two or three Charms to do the same thing. As far as I know, Earth-Aspected DBs do not have a Charm that lets them tunnel through solid earth, but an Earth Elemental could with the appropriate Charm. Does this not seem strange?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be surprised to see more DB charms for manipulating their element <i>to an extent</i> -- Earth-aspect DBs did get a climbing charm that caused stone and earth to make handholds for them, and it's not unreasonable for them to get a tunnel-making or earthworks-raising charm in Craft.<br /> <br /> However, I think you're misunderstanding what the DBs are. They are not elemental deities or Nobilis-style masters of an elemental domain; they are heroic swords-and-sandals demigods whose powers <i>express</i> themselves through raw elemental essence. A typical Fire Aspect, say, might be a swordsman who burns with unnatural fire when his passions rise and who leaves streaks of flame behind him when he swings his sword full-force; and he might be able to harness this power to draw forth a sword of elemental fire or to fling bolts of flame.<br /> <br /> But the crux of his power's expressions are based around the concept of heroic human talent as realized through fire-aspected Essence, not &quot;master of all things fire&quot;; the DB charmset is not friendly to someone who wants to ignore swordsmanship (or whatever) entirely and just &quot;do fire stuff.&quot; And similarly, for the most part, a DB's command over the elements exists at the points where it intersects with their heroic skill, rather than being a sorcery-style unnatural art that they can apply to whatever they desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T04:39:25-08:00","id":330014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329942#post329942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is indeed the impression left on me by the previous editions' mechanics. I get absolutely no impression of actual <i>connection</i>, on <i>any</i> level, to the elements of the world from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no memory of that being said anywhere in the line, and I'm incredulous that you've interpreted it that way. I certainly haven't, and apparently, I'm not the only one.<br /> <br /> I think you can certainly water a plant with your bolt of water. It's probably going to damage the plant, thought, being a combat charm and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T06:42:00-08:00","id":330085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329946#post329946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... they are heroic swords-and-sandals demigods whose powers <i>express</i> themselves through raw elemental essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that's why I've never really been interested in playing the DBs, really. Because, to me, that's boring. This also explains why I like playing <i>Mage</i> so much wherein I can be an enlightened mortal whose power can generate, manipulate or snuff out raw elemental essence (among other things) to virtually any effect I can imagine.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the DBs are similar to the Solar Exalted but instead of having sunlight and other solar iconography in their aesthetics, it's elements. Which is a bit of a tease, for me. It's dangling the imagery and potential for element-shaping in front of my face but then saying, &quot;No, no. They don't actually work like that.&quot; Their outward presentation has always spoken to me of elemental demi-gods, not demi-gods whose cosmetic expressions are elementally-themed. You're correct, I've misunderstood them entirely and now that I have had it cleared up for me I can honestly say that I want nothing to do with Dragon-Blooded in my Creation. For the purposes of my games, I'll replace them entirely with god-blooded or enlightened mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T07:01:03-08:00","id":330098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329354#post329354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A related thought: a lot of the reason so many DB charms involve conjuring, rather than manipulating, elements, is because requiring you to have the element on-hand would be a hassle, and one that disproportionately burdens specific Aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, this is a point I was never entirely clear on for the Ryujin...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T07:03:49-08:00","id":330100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330085#post330085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their outward presentation has always spoken to me of elemental demi-gods, not demi-gods whose cosmetic expressions are elementally-themed. You're correct, I've misunderstood them entirely and now that I have had it cleared up for me I can honestly say that I want nothing to do with Dragon-Blooded in my Creation. For the purposes of my games, I'll replace them entirely with god-blooded or enlightened mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious - where do you think this false impression came from?<br /> <br /> I used to understand DBs as being like Benders, for which I blame a series of demotivational posters that equated DBs with characters from Avatar, usually from the Fire Nation. My Exalted gaming experiences rarely involved DBs until eventually I made one myself, so I carried around that misunderstanding for a while.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T07:03:59-08:00","id":330101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330085#post330085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe that's why I've never really been interested in playing the DBs, really. Because, to me, that's boring. This also explains why I like playing <i>Mage</i> so much wherein I can be an enlightened mortal whose power can generate, manipulate or snuff out raw elemental essence (among other things) to virtually any effect I can imagine.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the DBs are similar to the Solar Exalted but instead of having sunlight and other solar iconography in their aesthetics, it's elements. Which is a bit of a tease, for me. It's dangling the imagery and potential for element-shaping in front of my face but then saying, &quot;No, no. They don't actually work like that.&quot; Their outward presentation has always spoken to me of elemental demi-gods, not demi-gods whose cosmetic expressions are elementally-themed. You're correct, I've misunderstood them entirely and now that I have had it cleared up for me I can honestly say that I want nothing to do with Dragon-Blooded in my Creation. For the purposes of my games, I'll replace them entirely with god-blooded or enlightened mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we no longer using the phrase &quot;weird hill to die on&quot;?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T07:26:43-08:00","id":330108,"title":"","content":"This is insane to me. So air aspect animas don't flutter their clothing in the breeze or shear wooden doors, fire aspect animas don't set the terrain ablaze, the wood aspect poison is actually some kind of essence thing and not literally a poison on your fists? Apparently I've been so wrong for so long. In my games an epic mid battle speech by an air aspect is totally punctuated by an arc flash of lightning and a crack of thunder. An earth aspects MA attack is totally accompanied by his sandstorm anima helping to blind his target. Nothing beyond a stunt, but totally physical.<br /> <br /> If that's wrong then I actually agree with Wulf. DBs suck, x-blooded and exigents all the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T07:44:27-08:00","id":330122,"title":"","content":"Going back and reading BOTH editions descriptions of Anima Flux, Aspect Markings and Anima Powers...Valles and/or Wulf is pretty much correct, at least regarding those things. Note the use of &quot;phantom&quot; and &quot;phantasmal&quot; in those passages. The above described duel between Wood Aspects, in particular, would NOT leave plant life all over the place.<br /> <br /> The major exception is the Fire anima, which 2E notes will ignite inflammable materials. All the other anima banners do the exact same amount and *type* of damage, to soft woods, people and such, no matter what element that they are supposedly manifesting.<br /> <br /> OTOH, the elemental markings are presented as mostly real; the Wood aspect can give someone the flowers growing out of her head. But the snow and ice settling around an Air aspect would fade away, although you could get chilly from the breeze. No mention is made of things getting wet around a Water aspect at all.<br /> <br /> Hm, not sure what would happen if an Air aspect activated their anima in total vacuum...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 12-04-2014, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T07:50:25-08:00","id":330127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330108#post330108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is insane to me. So air aspect animas don't flutter their clothing in the breeze or shear wooden doors, fire aspect animas don't set the terrain ablaze, the wood aspect poison is actually some kind of essence thing and not literally a poison on your fists? Apparently I've been so wrong for so long. In my games an epic mid battle speech by an air aspect is totally punctuated by an arc flash of lightning and a crack of thunder. An earth aspects MA attack is totally accompanied by his sandstorm anima helping to blind his target. Nothing beyond a stunt, but totally physical.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>1st edition is clear that the Air lightening is phantasmal, yes. 2nd edition...the wording is less clear. Not sure about the poison, as it does linger in the victim's systems even after the anima is shut off, so it's probably real? Yes, fire animas do set the terrain ablaze, if it can be set ablaze in the first place. The sandstorm would be effectively an insubstantial illusion, RAW.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note that charms like Elemental Armor Technique, however, DO conjure the real elements for their effects. Unless the 1000 Correct Errata changed this, I haven't checked it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 12-04-2014, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T07:56:24-08:00","id":330129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=329303#post329303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The offending quote lies at the bottom of the sidebar on page 33 of CoCD: Yu Shan.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, yeah, that is pretty bad. I could work with it if it didn't claim that Gods are essentially programmed to &quot;instinctively&quot; hold the DBs in contempt, but...ugh, Do Not Want!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T08:12:58-08:00","id":330160,"title":"","content":"Actually, I misread the Wood aspect duel as being about the anima banner, when really it was about Elemental Bolt Attack. First Edition describes this as a &quot;bolt&quot; of elemental force, manifesting as a lance of wood (which we see the Roseblack use in chapter fiction) or crystal or what have you. Second describes a bolt of energy with an elemental after effect. The Fire only burns for a single action, but I'm unclear if the seawater that chokes the target just vanishes after you spit it out. The Wood aspect is a plant toxin that affects one for the remainder of the scene. <br /> <br /> The real question is for charms like Dragon Seared Battlefield and Dragon Vortex Attack: Do the swirling gusts of flame, ice crystals, grinding dust and pollen, and stinging briar patches these charms conjure linger after the charm is shut off? Difficult to say...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T08:21:25-08:00","id":330171,"title":"","content":"More power = more permanence, presumably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T08:22:02-08:00","id":330174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330122#post330122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note the use of &quot;phantom&quot; and &quot;phantasmal&quot; in those passages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I took this mostly as a no hijinks clause.<br /> There is a very physical manifestation of the Dragon-Blooded's power in anima flux. So the Earth Aspect would cause tremors and have debris swirling around them but they wouldn't be considerably richer just because their totemic anima consisted of diamonds floating around them, that would be silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T08:44:35-08:00","id":330189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330085#post330085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe that's why I've never really been interested in playing the DBs, really. Because, to me, that's boring. This also explains why I like playing <i>Mage</i> so much wherein I can be an enlightened mortal whose power can generate, manipulate or snuff out raw elemental essence (among other things) to virtually any effect I can imagine.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the DBs are similar to the Solar Exalted but instead of having sunlight and other solar iconography in their aesthetics, it's elements. Which is a bit of a tease, for me. It's dangling the imagery and potential for element-shaping in front of my face but then saying, &quot;No, no. They don't actually work like that.&quot; Their outward presentation has always spoken to me of elemental demi-gods, not demi-gods whose cosmetic expressions are elementally-themed. You're correct, I've misunderstood them entirely and now that I have had it cleared up for me I can honestly say that I want nothing to do with Dragon-Blooded in my Creation. For the purposes of my games, I'll replace them entirely with god-blooded or enlightened mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think saying that they're &quot;similar to the Solar Exalted&quot; isn't quite on-the-nose. That's just how the Exalted work, as a group. The Solar Exalted are the purest expression of it, but it's more an &quot;Exalted thing&quot; than a &quot;Solar thing&quot;. The character of the individual Exalted is not merely aesthetic/cosmetic, but it seldom diverges as far from the baseline as what you seem to want. Not giving its main protagonists Mage-style powers on tap is a deliberate design decision that has subtle interactions with a number of the game's aesthetic and philosophical premises. I'm sorry that you assumed the &quot;elemental Exalted&quot; would rely on generalized elemental manipulation and were let down by the reality, but I don't think you can really blame the game for being misleading, because there's nothing about &quot;the character type with elemental abilities&quot; that implies that.<br /> <br /> There's clearly leeway to mess with this with Exigents, but my inclination would be to go for god-blooded or raksha for what you're after, or to look for it in another RPG. Which isn't meant as a &quot;my way or the highway&quot; statement, it's just that the game is built around a conscious rejection of the specific thing you want, so it's going to be hard to find a satisfactory compromise there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T10:08:19-08:00","id":330270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330174#post330174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I took this mostly as a no hijinks clause.<br /> There is a very physical manifestation of the Dragon-Blooded's power in anima flux. So the Earth Aspect would cause tremors and have debris swirling around them but they wouldn't be considerably richer just because their totemic anima consisted of diamonds floating around them, that would be silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I also enforce. Water aspects can die of thirst in a wasteland, earth aspects can't use anima diamonds for money, ect. It's just sort of understood that if you want your badass wood aspect to leave a trail of lush greenery or deadly thorns in her wake that you can't abuse it. Otherwise you lose your cool toy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T10:35:25-08:00","id":330311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330270#post330270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This I also enforce. Water aspects can die of thirst in a wasteland, earth aspects can't use anima diamonds for money, ect. It's just sort of understood that if you want your badass wood aspect to leave a trail of lush greenery or deadly thorns in her wake that you can't abuse it. Otherwise you lose your cool toy.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I don't see how having 'elemental' abilities can have any other <i>point</i>. If we're not allowed to actually <i>use</i> the tools we're given, <i>why play the game at all</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T11:02:57-08:00","id":330346,"title":"","content":"Because it's a significant reward or punishment for something as simple character aesthetic.<br /> One Earth Aspect has an infinite supply of diamonds, the other has an infinite supply of sand...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 12-04-2014, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T11:36:15-08:00","id":330382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330311#post330311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...I don't see how having 'elemental' abilities can have any other <i>point</i>. If we're not allowed to actually <i>use</i> the tools we're given, <i>why play the game at all</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure, undiluted stunt fodder and cool factor. An earth aspect who's anima is just flashy white light showing badgers is kind of meh, all you can do with that is describe how flashy it is or the shapes it takes, an earth aspect who stunts a jump as planting his feet and then leaping up as the earth itself heaves and hurls his body into the air. The cool thing is that by the rules of exalted that's actually mechanically better than just jumping, but you didn't use a charm purchase to get the coolness of it.<br /> <br /> What other exalt gets to do that with their anima? Only alchemicals and even then only a bit. Meanwhile my water aspect boss is over here stunting a charge Attack as riding a tidal wave of his anima forwards and surfing it by his target while slashing with his dire lance. That kind of aesthetic is kind of the reason to play a DB when other exalts would do, assuming evocations don't fuck that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T13:32:20-08:00","id":330504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330189#post330189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry that you assumed the &quot;elemental Exalted&quot; would rely on generalized elemental manipulation and were let down by the reality, but I don't think you can really blame the game for being misleading, because there's nothing about &quot;the character type with elemental abilities&quot; that implies that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems I really have completely misunderstood the Dragon-Blooded. I wasn't reading carefully enough but, in my defense, there are places in the game line that have contributed to my misunderstanding such as:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every Dragon-Blood belongs to one of five elemental aspects that correspond to the Elemental Dragons of Air, Earth, Fire, Water and Wood. Aspect gives the character a spiritual and physical bond with that particular element, which reveals itself in her appearance, her talents and the powers she wields as a member of the Dragon-Blooded Host.<br /> <br /> Nothing impacts the life of a Terrestrial Exalt so much as the Elemental Dragon whose power she channels.<br /> <br /> - Manual of Exalted Power: The Dragon-Blooded, page 96 </div> </div> </div>And...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The spiritual impact of having an elemental aspect rather than a caste cannot be overstated.<br /> <br /> - Manual of Exalted Power: The Dragon-Blooded, page 126 </div> </div> </div>I feel as though it <i>has </i>been overstated.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T13:45:14-08:00","id":330511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing impacts the life of a Terrestrial Exalt so much as the Elemental Dragon whose power she channels. </div> </div> </div>Well, that's somewhere between hyperbole and an outright lie.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T13:48:24-08:00","id":330512,"title":"","content":"In 1e, when what are now known as Excellencies had their own write-ups as individual Charms, Dragon-Blooded excellencies were usually elemental manipulation powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T13:56:04-08:00","id":330518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330511#post330511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's somewhere between hyperbole and an outright lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's lines like this that have led me to believe that the Dragon-Blooded actually used elemental powers rather than powers with elemental themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T14:01:15-08:00","id":330523,"title":"","content":"Wait I'm confused now, are people suggesting that Dragon Graced Weapon deals extra damage because the aspect of fire is painful and damaging and therefore your sword, life fire, deals more damage? Because I'm pretty sure that shit deals extra damage because it's fucking on fire and cutting you. Likewise the water version doesn't slow your opponent with the restricting element of water, they literally drown for a few seconds. Again it's not explicit it's just how I always imagined it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T16:34:17-08:00","id":330594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330311#post330311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I don't see how having 'elemental' abilities can have any other <i>point</i>. If we're not allowed to actually <i>use</i> the tools we're given, <i>why play the game at all</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, remember, in this case we're just talking about your unique anima expression. Compare it to a Twilight, say -- I might have my anima consist of fluttering pages containing secret knowledge, which is cool. But then turning around and saying &quot;all right, I glance at those fluttering pages and learn this secret from them&quot; is not cool (except maybe as a stunt to justify a Lore roll I could make anyway.) Players shouldn't get disproportionate rewards for how they describe their anima, or you're both devaluing any charms that do similar things and encouraging them to chose their anima tactically.<br /> <br /> That said, remember that the things you want to do aren't necessarily <i>impossible</i>; you just need a charm for them. Bringing forth water or lush greenery in the desert is a logical thing for some DB charms of the appropriate aspects to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330518#post330518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's lines like this that have led me to believe that the Dragon-Blooded actually used elemental powers rather than powers with elemental themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do use elemental powers, really. It's just that their elemental powers are primarily built around this concept of elemental swords-and-sandal heroes. (People usually describe it as &quot;elemental supersoldiers&quot;, but supersoldiers makes them sound like space marines or something.) They channel elemental power through their talents.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you shouldn't give up completely on what you want. 3e is still going to have them be Ability-based, but it's also going to allow you to make powers of all five elements in every Ability, which opens up a lot more room for powers -- for example, above, you asked about using your power over Earth to dig a tunnel, and I mentioned that that's something you could probably do in 2e because it fits into Craft and matches their other Craft charms; but in 2e, you couldn't have them use Craft to create a wall of flames. (At least, not easily -- you could probably create a 'raise earthworks' charm and then have an option to invoke it with other elements, but it would be clunky.)<br /> <br /> In 3e you'll probably be able to do something like that a lot more easily. But the game is still built to have you specialize along the lines defined by your mortal skills -- you can't easily be a generic &quot;master of all things fire&quot;, since DBs are something more specific than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-04-2014, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T16:46:08-08:00","id":330617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330085#post330085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe that's why I've never really been interested in playing the DBs, really. Because, to me, that's boring. This also explains why I like playing <i>Mage</i> so much wherein I can be an enlightened mortal whose power can generate, manipulate or snuff out raw elemental essence (among other things) to virtually any effect I can imagine.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the DBs are similar to the Solar Exalted but instead of having sunlight and other solar iconography in their aesthetics, it's elements. Which is a bit of a tease, for me. It's dangling the imagery and potential for element-shaping in front of my face but then saying, &quot;No, no. They don't actually work like that.&quot; Their outward presentation has always spoken to me of elemental demi-gods, not demi-gods whose cosmetic expressions are elementally-themed. You're correct, I've misunderstood them entirely and now that I have had it cleared up for me I can honestly say that I want nothing to do with Dragon-Blooded in my Creation. For the purposes of my games, I'll replace them entirely with god-blooded or enlightened mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the 1st Edition Dragonblooded Aspect books?<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded don't manipulate the elements the way that, ahem, some other fantasy setting does, but I wouldn't go far enough to say that Solar&gt;Sun = same as Dragonblooded&gt;Elements.<br /> <br /> For the Dragonblooded their elemental aspect is as much a psychology and philosophy (I doubt there's any difference between the two in Creation) as it is an &quot;expression&quot;. Fire aspect Dragonblooded are taught the value of restraint and discipline lest their burning passions destroy themselves and others (which, I'll admit, is a little reminiscent of that other fantasy setting) Earth Aspects are encouraged to change and grow, Water to conserve their energy for the perfect strike.*<br /> <br /> They're nuanced characters, and the elements reflect and refract the way the see Creation and themselves, not just some collection of powers. Some of them believe themselves to be inherently more enlightened* than mortals, and that their element-founded mindset is above mortal thinking in the same way that mortal thinking is above animals. Almost all of them believe they know what's best for Creation (generally, the Dragonblooded). Although they stride across Creation as the Princes of the Earth they have passions and appetites that cannot be matched by mortal individuals.<br /> <br /> Before you throw them out, I urge you to take a second look at them knowing that they're emphatically -not- elemental benders, nor element themed minor Solars, and see how you like them as they are.<br /> <br /> (*Keeping in mind that in setting, enlightenment runs closer to 1970's Communist China Party Doctrine than actual enlightenment as wisdom)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":". 12-06-2014, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T17:03:22-08:00","id":330624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330504#post330504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems I really have completely misunderstood the Dragon-Blooded. I wasn't reading carefully enough but, in my defense, there are places in the game line that have contributed to my misunderstanding such as:<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <br /> Every Dragon-Blood belongs to one of five elemental aspects that correspond to the Elemental Dragons of Air, Earth, Fire, Water and Wood. Aspect gives the character a spiritual and physical bond with that particular element, which reveals itself in her appearance, her talents and the powers she wields as a member of the Dragon-Blooded Host.<br /> <br /> Nothing impacts the life of a Terrestrial Exalt so much as the Elemental Dragon whose power she channels.<br /> <br /> - Manual of Exalted Power: The Dragon-Blooded, page 96</span><br /> </i></span><br /> <br /> And...<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <br /> The spiritual impact of having an elemental aspect rather than a caste cannot be overstated.<br /> <br /> - Manual of Exalted Power: The Dragon-Blooded, page 126</span><br /> </i></span><br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>In one sense, this is hyperbole. In another sense, this is more a case of bad translation from 1E to 2E. MoEP thinks that the Dragonblooded are humans* with elemental powers.<br /> <br /> They're not. Not anymore than Solar are humans* who happen to cop the powers of The Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded do not manipulate their element, they are their element; the essence of that element is entwined with how they think, the foods they favor, who they find attractive, which skills they naturally excel at. A Fire Aspect who activates Comet Deflecting Technique is <i>burning with the grace of fire </i>as she interposes her weapon to block an attack, the Air aspects voice <i>is the flowing wind travelling miles distant</i> to send a dire warning or a chilling secret.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded's elemental aspect is incredibly important. I wouldn't go so far as to say it's the 'most important thing' (because who the hell knows what makes us people?) but I would say it's a hell of an important thing. The elemental aesthetic of the Dragonblood is not there to lead one to think of individuals who manipulate their element (though some charms may express themselves this way), the elemental aesthetic is there to reinforce the influence that the Dragonblooded's aspect has on who they are as an individual.<br /> <br /> *Of course Dragonblooded and Solar are humans. They get lonely-hungry-horny-sleepy-giddy, but they tend to do it in extreme ways. And an Exalt that controls their passions is showing an amount of self-restraint that's mind-boggling. But one should be reminded that the Exalted are not merely people with powers**<br /> <br /> **Or maybe they are, and people just tend to act extravagant and crazy when they have incredible power. It's kind of one of the big questions of Exalted. It's probably ineffable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T17:44:10-08:00","id":330657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330382#post330382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pure, undiluted stunt fodder and cool factor. An earth aspect who's anima is just flashy white light showing badgers is kind of meh, all you can do with that is describe how flashy it is or the shapes it takes, an earth aspect who stunts a jump as planting his feet and then leaping up as the earth itself heaves and hurls his body into the air. The cool thing is that by the rules of exalted that's actually mechanically better than just jumping, but you didn't use a charm purchase to get the coolness of it.<br /> <br /> What other exalt gets to do that with their anima? Only alchemicals and even then only a bit. Meanwhile my water aspect boss is over here stunting a charge Attack as riding a tidal wave of his anima forwards and surfing it by his target while slashing with his dire lance. That kind of aesthetic is kind of the reason to play a DB when other exalts would do, assuming evocations don't fuck that up.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I..<br /> <br /> ...How is that <i>less</i> broken than having your powers <i>actually be what they're billed as</i>? <b><i>WHAT?!</i></b><br /> <br /> It's <i>nonsense.</i> They're <i>exactly the same thing</i>.<br /> <br /> I... Sorry, I can't think of any calmer way to put it right now. I'll edit this if I manage to think of one, it's just... <i>What</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T18:06:53-08:00","id":330678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330518#post330518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's lines like this that have led me to believe that the Dragon-Blooded actually used elemental powers rather than powers with elemental themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a somewhat artificial distinction, and not one implied by the passages you cited, but running with it, they have always had some of both, albeit not as many of the former as might be ideal (largely a function of the fact that their charmset was small, and there are a lot of meat-and-potatoes powers that &quot;bending&quot; doesn't cover). But even having said all that, it doesn't really have <i>anything</i> to do with whether they have generalized &quot;bending&quot; or not. Dragon-Blooded with nothing but physical, literalist element manipulation would still have it divided into narrowly-focused ability charms.<br /> <br /> The impression I'm getting here is that you had a specific vision of what &quot;the guys with elemental powers&quot; looked like, and you were into that, and you read stuff that talked about the Dragon-Blooded being elemental and took it as corroboration. But I think this is mostly assumptions you brought to the table yourself, because it's not really even in the passages you cited <i>specifically</i>.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with being mistaken, especially in a game like Exalted which has subtle and convoluted presentation and is usually pitched poorly. But it's not a failing of the game that it happened, either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330657#post330657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...I..<br /> <br /> ...How is that <i>less</i> broken than having your powers <i>actually be what they're billed as</i>? <b><i>WHAT?!</i></b><br /> <br /> It's <i>nonsense.</i> They're <i>exactly the same thing</i>.<br /> <br /> I... Sorry, I can't think of any calmer way to put it right now. I'll edit this if I manage to think of one, it's just... <i>What</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>DB powers are pretty much what they're billed as, aside from the &quot;cooperation&quot; aspect which never really worked. I have yet to see a remotely compelling case made for the game actually misrepresenting Dragon-Blooded in this respect. Perhaps you can be the first!<br /> <br /> To answer the non-loaded part of your question, though: the reason stunts that let you do anything are better than powers that let you do anything is because stunts are subject to heavy ST control and they therefore don't have most of the unpleasant edge cases and undesirable setting extrapolations that you get by making those things Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 12-04-2014, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T18:09:03-08:00","id":330681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330624#post330624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one sense, this is hyperbole. In another sense, this is more a case of bad translation from 1E to 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you know that it was bad translation and not an intentional shift?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T18:25:07-08:00","id":330691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330681#post330681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you know that it was bad translation and not an intentional shift?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the land of pretending to be an elf I'd rather err on the side of 'author didn't understand what they were talking about' than 'author making the game worse'*. <br /> <br /> And since the 2nd Edition DB writer was not the 1st Edition DB writer, I don't especially feel any loyalty towards their interpretation.**<br /> <br /> *Of course, mileage of worse is relative etc-etc-etc<br /> **Which I believe to be, frankly, pretty dumb. See asterisk above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T18:31:55-08:00","id":330692,"title":"","content":"While I'm usually down with criticizing 2nd Edition, I think the Dragon-Blooded book was great.<br /> <br /> (Unless that's where the 900 males to 100 females story came from. If so, I'm going to have to deduct a star.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T18:34:31-08:00","id":330694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330692#post330692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Unless that's where the 900 males to 100 females story came from. If so, I'm going to have to deduct a star.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the other way around (9900 women, 100 men) and I think that was from DotFA (appropriately enough).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T18:35:32-08:00","id":330695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330678#post330678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DB powers are pretty much what they're billed as, aside from the &quot;cooperation&quot; aspect which never really worked. I have yet to see a remotely compelling case made for the game actually misrepresenting Dragon-Blooded in this respect. Perhaps you can be the first!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Wulf's already covered it, frankly - DBs are described in their introduction and aspect fluff as being intimately tied to their elements, and then in practice they end up with 'phantasmal' special effects around far more generic abilities. That said, this isn't the point that has me exercised...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330678#post330678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To answer the non-loaded part of your question, though: the reason stunts that let you do anything are better than powers that let you do anything is because stunts are subject to heavy ST control and they therefore don't have most of the unpleasant edge cases and undesirable setting extrapolations that you get by making those things Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and actually, neither is this, given that my objections to it aren't really germane to this discussion.<br /> <br /> What has me so incredulous is the way people seem to be completely ignoring the blatant self-contradiction involved in claiming that 'surfing on a self-created tidal wave' is both a difference in <i>kind </i>from 'filling a glass from your anima' or 'catching a waterskin by the water inside it', and somehow <i>less</i> disruptive. <i>That</i>, I don't understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T18:38:27-08:00","id":330696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330694#post330694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the other way around (9900 women, 100 men) and I think that was from DotFA (appropriately enough).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I had that backwards, my bad.<br /> <br /> I'm glad it was from a book I don't recall liking much to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T18:50:55-08:00","id":330700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330692#post330692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm usually down with criticizing 2nd Edition, I think the Dragon-Blooded book was great.<br /> <br /> (Unless that's where the 900 males to 100 females story came from. If so, I'm going to have to deduct a star.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, I don't really remember much about MoEP: Dragonblooded. <br /> <br /> Aspect Book (Element), those I remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T18:54:19-08:00","id":330702,"title":"","content":"No, it's absolutely in MoEP: Dragon-Blooded. Page 50, section heading The Origin of the Dragon-Blooded Host.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T19:32:45-08:00","id":330716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330695#post330695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Wulf's already covered it, frankly - DBs are described in their introduction and aspect fluff as being intimately tied to their elements, and then in practice they end up with 'phantasmal' special effects around far more generic abilities. That said, this isn't the point that has me exercised.</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>are</i> intimately tied to their elements, though, it's just that you don't consider &quot;Fire Aspects embody the essence and nature of fire, and have charms which create fire or involve behaving like fire&quot; as being &quot;intimately tied to the element&quot;, even when there are a few more direct manifestations to go with it. I submit that this is an arbitrary distinction based on your personal image of what &quot;elemental powers&quot; should be like. It's like playing a game where the characters are based on the four humours, and then objecting that the Bile Aspect isn't mostly about playing bile-benders, as you'd been led to presume.<br /> <br /> A substantial minority of DB powers are basically just &quot;powers the Exalted need to have, and they're tied to this element because that's the element that matches the Ability&quot;. But that's by no means the overarching theme of their charmset: a <i>lot</i> of the powers that don't involve overt manifestations of the element, or that do but not to your satisfaction, are very clearly channelling the element in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What has me so incredulous is the way people seem to be completely ignoring the blatant self-contradiction involved in claiming that 'surfing on a self-created tidal wave' is both a difference in <i>kind </i>from 'filling a glass from your anima' or 'catching a waterskin by the water inside it', and somehow <i>less</i> disruptive. <i>That</i>, I don't understand. </div> </div> </div>There's some truth to this, but it's not the abject double standard you're making it out to be, I don't think. Broad utility powers are dicey because they're expansive, and they tend to distort the setting in the same way as other potent utilitarian technology (which is functionally what they are). They also call the setting to account -- if Earth aspects can easily create significant amounts of money, for instance, it's hard to justify the Dragon-Blooded considering that thing valuable. If you've decided in advance that you want the setting to be a certain way, the bits and bobs have to fall into line with that vision, or else you get the kind of situation we've sometimes had in the past where a common power trivializes a problem the setting presents as serious, and the answer to that is &quot;eh, what can you do&quot;.<br /> <br /> Using elemental powers to enhance things that Dragon-Blooded, and the Exalted in general, are already established as doing, presents fewer obstacles and therefore demands less care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T20:55:02-08:00","id":330745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330716#post330716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They <i>are</i> intimately tied to their elements, though, it's just that you don't consider &quot;Fire Aspects embody the essence and nature of fire, and have charms which create fire or involve behaving like fire&quot; as being &quot;intimately tied to the element&quot;, even when there are a few more direct manifestations to go with it. I submit that this is an arbitrary distinction based on your personal image of what &quot;elemental powers&quot; should be like. It's like playing a game where the characters are based on the four humours, and then objecting that the Bile Aspect isn't mostly about playing bile-benders, as you'd been led to presume.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no I don't think it is. Even if I accepted your parallel, the difference in degree between the range of interesting play options cut off by blocking 'bile bending' and those involved in blocking interaction with physical elements is so great as to keep it from being a useful comparison.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330716#post330716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A substantial minority of DB powers are basically just &quot;powers the Exalted need to have, and they're tied to this element because that's the element that matches the Ability&quot;. But that's by no means the overarching theme of their charmset: a <i>lot</i> of the powers that don't involve overt manifestations of the element, or that do but not to your satisfaction, are very clearly channelling the element in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no objection to large parts, even a majority, of the charmset not involving overt manifestations. I <i>do</i> object to the thesis that the physical aspects of the meaning of, say, Air, should be sidelined and minimized in the fashion that they currently are - to the <i>only</i> region where physicality is allowed being stunts that require deliberately contradicting the established mechanical basis of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330716#post330716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's some truth to this, but it's not the abject double standard you're making it out to be, I don't think. Broad utility powers are dicey because they're expansive, and they tend to distort the setting in the same way as other potent utilitarian technology (which is functionally what they are). They also call the setting to account -- if Earth aspects can easily create significant amounts of money, for instance, it's hard to justify the Dragon-Blooded considering that thing valuable. If you've decided in advance that you want the setting to be a certain way, the bits and bobs have to fall into line with that vision, or else you get the kind of situation we've sometimes had in the past where a common power trivializes a problem the setting presents as serious, and the answer to that is &quot;eh, what can you do&quot;.<br /> <br /> Using elemental powers to enhance things that Dragon-Blooded, and the Exalted in general, are already established as doing, presents fewer obstacles and therefore demands less care.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall a point being made about how 'physical elemental manipulation in one charm' is a separate discussion from 'including physical elements in charms of the same scope as less physical charms'. If I wanted to make the former argument, I'd be starting a new thread about how one very flexible 48XP charm is a superior play experience to six 8XP charms that add up to about the same standard applications - as I haven't, so far.<br /> <br /> In the one I'm actually making, and taking your example of monetary Earth Aspects, I'd figure that animas would by default produce the commonest denominator of their elements - an Earth Aspect who glittered like a faceted constellation would be producing cubic zirconia or something else far more common than diamonds, and that the monetary value of what you <i>could</i> get out of charm manifestations would be linked to either other charms, more difficult gates like permanent essence, or, most likely, both.<br /> <br /> Given dev statements about how the biggest difficulty with charm design in the new system is coming up with ideas for what to do, I doubt that this represents an increase in complexity sufficient to outweigh the number of plot and play options it introduces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","user":"Valles","date":". 12-05-2014, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T23:08:34-08:00","id":330801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330695#post330695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What has me so incredulous is the way people seem to be completely ignoring the blatant self-contradiction involved in claiming that 'surfing on a self-created tidal wave' is both a difference in <i>kind </i>from 'filling a glass from your anima' or 'catching a waterskin by the water inside it', and somehow <i>less</i> disruptive. <i>That</i>, I don't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically I kind of treat it like this. Doing really cool stuff like pulling your anima in and encasing your body in diamond for the purpose of stunting a feat of strength to hold up a falling building is awesome, and it kind of feels lame if it's not actually happening. Likewise it feels lame if I have to stunt it as cubic zirconia or something. It would also really suck if I had to take a charm that let me manipulate my element in cool ways to be able to do that. I don't want to sink all my starting bonus points into something just to be able to do cool stuff with my element. On the other hand being able to use elemental manifestations for whatever the hell other than stunts, like a water aspect providing enough drinkable water for a village out in the wastes simply through having a water anima then that's too flexible to be a part of simply your anima.<br /> <br /> Kind of like that joke everyone makes about Glorious Solar Desk. If you can make a sword or bow and armor out of hard light, where exactly is the difficulty in making literally anything else out of hard light? Why can't GSS make a table shaped sword, or a canoe shaped sword and just use that for whatever purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T23:14:08-08:00","id":330802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Originally posted by*Exalted: the Dragon-BloodedWhat Solar Exalted?Another valid approach is to ignore the Solar Exalted entirely, in many Dragon-Blooded stories they're unnecessary. The Realm is filled with many opportunities for adventure that have nothing to do with the Solars at all. Internecine conflict, religious debates and border clashes happen all the time - usually without the involvement of the Solars. You should never feel compelled to include any element of the setting that doesn't serve your purpose; if the addition of the Solars would upset your carefully laid series don't include them. It's just as reasonable to exclude them as it is to leave out the Guild, the Threshold or any element for which you have no use. Players usually introduce complications into stories on their own without the Storyteller's helping them. If the Solar Exalted would be another complication leave them be. </div> </div> </div>The absolute best advice possible.<br /> <br /> Rule zero fallacy my ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T23:18:50-08:00","id":330806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=327220#post327220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it looks like I'll have to continue my tradition of giving DB players the <i>Affinity (Element) Control</i> Spirit Charm, then. Having elementally-empowered heroes who cannot manipulate their own element will always seem backwards and weird to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make it a Lore charm and the amount of element one can manipulate is based on their permannt Essence score (compare the mass to the strength lifting chart or some such)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T23:54:30-08:00","id":330845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328442#post328442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always kind of themed that random effects like that could be accomplished by you stunting your anima, and in fact earth aspects do have a tunnelling charm in war, it might even be the first one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a brilliant idea. make controlling a DBs native element a basic function of their anima ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T00:42:23-08:00","id":330880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330694#post330694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the other way around (9900 women, 100 men) and I think that was from DotFA (appropriately enough).</div> </div> </div> </div>It was MoEP: Dragon-Blooded.<br /> DotFA only addressed the dilution of the bloodlines and offered a much more palatable explanation for how it happened than the Terrestrial Exalted Host being so universally horny that accidents were bound to happen answer we were initially given.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T00:46:45-08:00","id":330894,"title":"","content":"This is the sound of my heart breaking.<br /> <br /> Oh well, the book was mostly great then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T02:18:30-08:00","id":330928,"title":"","content":"What? No, those numbers make perfect sense. They were supposed to be making an army of dragonblooded to back up each solar. (They handle the army of devas while the solar goes for the fetich/jouten of the primordial) with just 10000 or so you're looking at about 33 apiece. That wouldn't do.<br /> <br /> If you want to make a lot of kids in the most efficient manner you need a lot of women and a handful of men, because you need an oven per bun but you have an almost endless supply of cake mix. It's just practical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 12-05-2014, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T03:07:38-08:00","id":330943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330695#post330695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What has me so incredulous is the way people seem to be completely ignoring the blatant self-contradiction involved in claiming that 'surfing on a self-created tidal wave' is both a difference in <i>kind </i>from 'filling a glass from your anima' or 'catching a waterskin by the water inside it', and somehow <i>less</i> disruptive. <i>That</i>, I don't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the same boat as why a Solar can make a shimmering sword from their soul or their Anima or ambient beams of sunlight without being able to just make anything out of them.<br /> <br /> Powers in Exalted are not reductive things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T03:13:20-08:00","id":330948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What? No, those numbers make perfect sense. They were supposed to be making an army of dragonblooded to back up each solar. (T<b>hey handle the army of devas while the solar goes for the fetich/jouten of the primordial)</b> with just 10000 or so you're looking at about 33 apiece. That wouldn't do. </div> </div> </div>So......the DB are Mook Exalted.......Since I'm not good with word I'm just gonna quote Sunder the Gold's post about the phenomenon of &quot;Your Mook killing Their Mook so the Glorious Main Character can finish the Big Bad&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the things I like -- and that sets it apart from just about every other shounen story I can remember -- is that the secondary hero actually delivered the death blow in one of their fights.<br /> <br /> I can't remember the last time an author showed a lick of restraint about having his beloved central character always being the one to land the final attack.<br /> <br /> Surely, Edgardo's uppercut against the unnamed lightning-throwing swordsman had the appropriate dramatic impact for the main character. It was the attack that showed the hero's growth and which turned the tide of the fight. But it didn't actually kill the enemy; it just left him open enough for A Guy Called Squid to kill him with his conventional-but-strong Fire Punch.<br /> <br /> Now, Squid eventually fell into the usual way of things, like their fight against Goldnharl, where he was the distraction and Edgardo got the final attack. Or Khaine, where Squid was paralyzed and unable to act, or Xer0, where Squid didn't even get to do anything before the game effectively ended.<br /> <br /> But at least once -- and possibly even more often, since most of their fights (the random encounters, and the training spars) -- Squid wasn't the second fiddle, the diversion, the booster rocket, or the meat-shield.<br /> <br /> Holy <i>shit</i>, I am sick of stories where only the main character really matters. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T03:21:11-08:00","id":330950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330928#post330928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to make a lot of kids in the most efficient manner</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not all that much about the Exalted that implies that efficiency was or could have been prioritized over some other things.<br /> <br /> Personally, I go with the idea that the very first Dragon Blooded were ten thousand individuals of an approximately even gender mix who managed to reach some sacred place (out of several million who heard the initial call and failed along the way), who by virtue of the nature of the journey had all come together and helped each other out long before making it there, where the Elemental Dragons revealed themselves and praised the strength of those who had made it and declared that they would be kin to them and blood to them for all time, and then they were Exalted. After that, little subgroups that had formed within them all travelled off in different directions to find their own way, but not before the whole lot of them affirmed their eternal kindred and they collectively pledged to meet again.<br /> <br /> A hundred years later, all of those groups were substantially larger, because human passions are what the are. Maybe they weren't as large as they could have been, but they were all pretty badass, so who cares. This was about the time when they started falling in with the Celestial Exalted.<br /> <br /> Not all of the original Ten Thousand lived to see each other again, but in the single battle in which all of the remaining ones came together and led the charge, it was a sight to behold.<br /> <br /> (Just to be clear, I mostly discount any references that explicit frame the Primordial War as having been a system where the Exalted were Chosen and then all immediately drawn into a kind of divine boot camp and then issued forth from an already established centralised and unified command structure as well. I imagine the circumstances of the War as a bit more mythic, although the Sidereals were always a fairly coherent host, and their actions helped coordinate distantly scattered Exalted of highly diverse technique.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T03:37:47-08:00","id":330955,"title":"","content":"I really don't consider &quot;doing most of the actual work&quot; not mattering.<br /> <br /> I mean they'd be fighting the mooks, yeah, but also the second circle demons and helping with the third circles and even the primordial jouten itself. The solar is really just the nuke needed to deal the finishing blow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 12-05-2014, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T05:23:40-08:00","id":331001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330955#post330955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't consider &quot;doing most of the actual work&quot; not mattering.<br /> <br /> I mean they'd be fighting the mooks, yeah, but also the second circle demons and helping with the third circles and even the primordial jouten itself. The solar is really just the nuke needed to deal the finishing blow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see why this should be the case, give the numbers. True, there is a large power gap between Dragon-Bloods and Solars, but it's not <i>that</i> wide, certainly not enough to make Solars of vital importance when they are outnumbered a thousand or more to one. Dragon-Blood Occult is just as capable of permanently killing demons as Solar Occult is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 12-05-2014, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T05:39:20-08:00","id":331008,"title":"","content":"When I consider what it might have meant for the Dragon Blooded to have fought so that the Solars and Lunars wouldn't be pinned down while they did their derring do, I don't think of orcs being mown down until Sauron takes the field, I think of the final stage of the Battle of Trost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T05:58:49-08:00","id":331013,"title":"","content":"Regardless of the exact mechanics, my point was that you'd need a shitload of them to do it. With solars, you need dbs to help clear a path through hordes of deva. Without solars, you <i>still</i> need dbs to clear a path through hordes of deva.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T06:26:22-08:00","id":331031,"title":"","content":"Re: anima effects, the way I'd tend to view it is that any diamonds in the anima are really diamonds, just that they are held together by the outflowing of the Dragonblood's essence and their soul, so they will collapse when that essence is withdrawn. Not exactly phantasmal, just not permanent or enduring independently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T06:49:47-08:00","id":331041,"title":"","content":"You should want to play a Dragonblooded if stories centering on the Realm interest you.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a superhuman hero without the extra cultural baggage of people often thinking of you as <i>possessed by Millennia old Demon-King.</i><br /> <br /> If running an empire sounds like fun, but you don't want to do all the work of building one from scratch.<br /> <br /> If you want to play up the drama of <i>Responsibility</i> and the <i>Mandate of Kings</i>. The Celestial Exalted may have more power, but these days when mortals are threatened by powers beyond them they will run to a Terrestrial rather than some Anathema.<br /> <br /> If political intrigue combined with a lineage-based power structure appeals to you, ala China, Egypt, or basically the entire Eastern Hemisphere up until WWI.<br /> <br /> If you want to roleplay what it's like to live in a world that tells you that you and your kin are infallible paragons of righteousness, yet you're daily witness to acts that contradict this, and one of your central conflicts consists of <i>do you give into the culture of sycophancy or fight against it</i>?<br /> <br /> And if the latter, will you continue to do so when that authority is the only thing standing between a safe and prosperous Satrapy and the carnage that comes from 300 years of simmering rebellious spirit?<br /> <br /> I think that's one of the central tenets of really interesting Dragonblooded games. The most righteous Dragonblooded are dedicated to a religion and philosophy that keeps people held down in misery*, but the most pragmatic (amoral) Dragonblood will happily abandon it, if it means their political advantage.<br /> <br /> So how do you save Creation while still staying true to yourself, and what ideals do you abandon or hold close in your pursuit of that end?<br /> <br /> Basically, there are a lot of interesting stories that only the Dragonblooded can tell. If one of those possible stories interest you, you should play a Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> If not, there are plenty of people that are interested by them, and there are plenty of other Exalt stories to play out instead.<br /> <br /> *The Realm/Immaculate Order does lots of good things too! But, their Empire and their peace is paid for in the blood, sweat, and self-determination of the Satrapies, the costs shouldn't be shied away from anymore than the costs of empire building should be white-washed in a Celestial game.<br /> <br /> **This makes for really interesting mixed Exalt games too, so long as you flatten the Exp costs and make sure that the Dragonblooded has a different niche focus than the Celestial players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":". 12-05-2014, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T08:11:02-08:00","id":331121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=328205#post328205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So yeah, Isator, you are correct. I don't see why I should think that the only two splats who got polished mechanics, continuing support throughout the edition, and weren't made into mooks were the favored sons of the edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it was just because it's easier and more straightforward to do so with the ones who are more straightforward, and then the ones who have represent compete Terra Incognita.<br /> <br /> But no, you're right, it's so much more likely, as well as contributing to a pleasant discussion atmosphere(!), to assume that misfires on the mechanics for other things were due to a bias against them that actually went into gleeful malicious hatred rather than it being a bit out of their reach and labouring under a misguided, if mildly understandable, development mandate to change as little as possible.<br /> <br /> It's just like how Dean Shomshak's writing of mechanically poor martial arts was because he hated martial arts and wanted all of us to hate it as well, rather than because he maybe wasn't the best choice to write martial arts mechanics. Let's all have a nice pleasant campfire in which we burn effigies of him, which will in no way make anybody feel brought down by association!<br /> <br /> Oh, wait, before we do that, we need to maybe find some way to fit the fact that the Alchemicals were the group with the best mechanics in the entire game into this paranoid reactionary model. Gonna need to stay up all night on this one...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T10:02:28-08:00","id":331247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330745#post330745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, no I don't think it is. Even if I accepted your parallel, the difference in degree between the range of interesting play options cut off by blocking 'bile bending' and those involved in blocking interaction with physical elements is so great as to keep it from being a useful comparison.<br /> <br /> I have no objection to large parts, even a majority, of the charmset not involving overt manifestations. I <i>do</i> object to the thesis that the physical aspects of the meaning of, say, Air, should be sidelined and minimized in the fashion that they currently are - to the <i>only</i> region where physicality is allowed being stunts that require deliberately contradicting the established mechanical basis of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how many times it needs to be said that nobody is suggesting blocking DBs' interaction with physical elements, and the DBs have never been portrayed as lacking that interaction. It is increasingly difficult to take you seriously when you just keep polishing this chestnut over and over again. As far as I can tell our disagreement is entirely about <i>degree, </i>and about how those powers should be handled within the system.<br /> <br /> I mean, I just do not know where you are getting this. Even the one passage you cited as an example of someone making this argument wasn't, and I've never seen it myself. I can totally believe there's like one or two people in the fandom who object strongly to that Earth charm that raises fortifications, or the Archery charm that grows arrows out of a tree or shrub, or the Melee charm where you summon a sword made out of ice and hitting people with it chills them to the bone, or whatever. However, if those are actually the people you object to then I wish you would take it up with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the one I'm actually making, and taking your example of monetary Earth Aspects, I'd figure that animas would by default produce the commonest denominator of their elements - an Earth Aspect who glittered like a faceted constellation would be producing cubic zirconia or something else far more common than diamonds, and that the monetary value of what you <i>could</i> get out of charm manifestations would be linked to either other charms, more difficult gates like permanent essence, or, most likely, both. </div> </div> </div>This isn't hugely bad, and I'd probably allow it as an unreliable cosmetic thing, but generally the way I would prefer to run it -- and I think the best compromise between elements -- is that the stuff that comes from anima flux is real but has a very short &quot;half-life&quot; and tends to dissolve into loose essence once you leave the area or tamp down your anima. This gives it a physicality without constraining your anima manifestation to &quot;stuff that won't screw up the setting if every same-Aspect DB can do it on demand.&quot;<br /> <br /> The basic problem here is that one doesn't want people using their anima <i>to</i> accomplish this stuff except as a rare neat trick that isn't presumed commonplace, which fits nicely into the stunting model. Even if DBs can do that stuff, doing it <i>through the anima</i> is often not good for the anima. For instance, the Solar anima tends to bleach things, and I would let a Solar stunt bleaching out bloodstains with their anima to evade the notice of police, but I wuld not make this an on-tap &quot;motes for bleach&quot; effect. You buy a charm for that. If it's useful and reliable to use your anima to whip up a bunch of raw materials, or reseed an orchard, or conjure enough water for your group to survive in the desert, that' s warping what the anima is to the point where I think it's lost its appeal as a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 12-05-2014, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T10:19:57-08:00","id":331263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331121#post331121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, wait, before we do that, we need to maybe find some way to fit the fact that the Alchemicals were the group with the best mechanics in the entire game into this paranoid reactionary model. Gonna need to stay up all night on this one...</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the Exalted books I've read have had an enormous problem with having no idea how to build heat for something without it being by bashing something else. Solars and Infernals are noticeably on the receiving end of this tendency far less than anyone else. Alchemicals escape it largely because they're in a disconnected setting and don't have to establish their place in the pecking order of the other Exalted. Even then MoEP: Alchemicals can't help but sneak a little bit of &quot;oh, but you'd need a Solar if you <i>really</i> wanted to get something done&quot; in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T10:39:29-08:00","id":331274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wulf</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>It seems I really have completely misunderstood the Dragon-Blooded. I wasn't reading carefully enough but, in my defense, there are places in the game line that have contributed to my misunderstanding such as:</i><br /> <br /> <i><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Every Dragon-Blood belongs to one of five elemental aspects that correspond to the Elemental Dragons of Air, Earth, Fire, Water and Wood. Aspect gives the character a spiritual and physical bond with that particular element, which reveals itself in her appearance, her talents and the powers she wields as a member of the Dragon-Blooded Host.<br /> <br /> Nothing impacts the life of a Terrestrial Exalt so much as the Elemental Dragon whose power she channels.<br /> <br /> - Manual of Exalted Power: The Dragon-Blooded, page 96</span></i></i><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>And...</i><br /> <br /> <i><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The spiritual impact of having an elemental aspect rather than a caste cannot be overstated.<br /> <br /> - Manual of Exalted Power: The Dragon-Blooded, page 126</span></i></i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330624#post330624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In one sense, this is hyperbole. In another sense, this is more a case of bad translation from 1E to 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaand this is where I am compelled to point out that this quote is copy-pasted from 1E's Exalted: the Dragon-Blooded (the first one, at least; haven't found the second one, but it wouldn't floor me with surprise to find it somewhere there). Not that the First Edition book is above hyperbole itself: &quot;By virtue of blood and birth, you are one of the Realm's ruling elite. By virtue of spiritual enlightenment, you are literally a bodhissatva among men, an enlightened saint destined to rule because of your divine might and spiritual advancement.&quot; (pg 146, and no, this passage is NOT presented as &quot;in-setting&quot;, it's talking right to the player). <br /> <br /> EtDB also has its moments of seeming contempt for its own subject, btw. Page 177 gives us this gem: &quot;...it's a simple fact that, in a <i>mano y mano</i> fight, the average Anathema will leave the average Dragon-Blooded lying in a pool of his own Exalted blood. In magic, as with everything else...the Dragon-Blooded are just not in the same league as the Solars.&quot;<br /> <br /> And there are certainly examples where DB charms have always been useless against magic, as Portentous Comet Deflecting Mode has always been ineffective &quot;against sorcery or attacks enhanced by Charms.&quot; 2E didn't make that up, although I'll grant it increased its frequency.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, since people apparentely forgot that it exists, there is Ramparts of Obedient Earth, an Earth-based War charm that allows the DB to stomp/punch the ground into various shapes, such as barriers against attacks, creating sinkholes for enemies to fall into, and, yes, to tunnel instantly through the ground...<br /> <br /> I have no defense for the DB breeding thing, however. That's totally on MoEP. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T10:45:13-08:00","id":331288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330801#post330801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically I kind of treat it like this. Doing really cool stuff like pulling your anima in and encasing your body in diamond for the purpose of stunting a feat of strength to hold up a falling building is awesome, and it kind of feels lame if it's not actually happening. Likewise it feels lame if I have to stunt it as cubic zirconia or something. It would also really suck if I had to take a charm that let me manipulate my element in cool ways to be able to do that. I don't want to sink all my starting bonus points into something just to be able to do cool stuff with my element. On the other hand being able to use elemental manifestations for whatever the hell other than stunts, like a water aspect providing enough drinkable water for a village out in the wastes simply through having a water anima then that's too flexible to be a part of simply your anima.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to have to invest immensely to do $CoolThing either. I just think it's preferable to having $CoolThing <i>not be something the game actually does</i>. 'You can stunt it' is just another way of putting 'You can house-rule it'... It's not terribly useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330801#post330801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of like that joke everyone makes about Glorious Solar Desk. If you can make a sword or bow and armor out of hard light, where exactly is the difficulty in making literally anything else out of hard light? Why can't GSS make a table shaped sword, or a canoe shaped sword and just use that for whatever purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I'm not sure what point this is trying to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330943#post330943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in the same boat as why a Solar can make a shimmering sword from their soul or their Anima or ambient beams of sunlight without being able to just make anything out of them.<br /> <br /> Powers in Exalted are not reductive things.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Huh. I'd never had a neat way of summarizing this tendency that I loathed before. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T11:26:04-08:00","id":331347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331274#post331274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, since people apparentely forgot that it exists, there is Ramparts of Obedient Earth, an Earth-based War charm that allows the DB to stomp/punch the ground into various shapes, such as barriers against attacks, creating sinkholes for enemies to fall into, and, yes, to tunnel instantly through the ground...</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately the time scale for that Spell is ridiculously impracticable for spontaneous use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T11:34:20-08:00","id":331354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331347#post331347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately the time scale for that Spell is ridiculously impracticable for spontaneous use.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're thinking of Raising The Earth's Bones. Ramparts of Obedient Earth is Reflexive Action-Only. It's pretty lacklustre until you hit E4, and then its auto-upgrade makes it incredibly effective. You can inflict knockdown by making sinkholes and make new cover and tunnels on the fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T11:35:14-08:00","id":331355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331347#post331347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately the time scale for that Spell is ridiculously impracticable for spontaneous use.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...What spell? It's a Reflexive, Instant War Charm (pg. 150, MoEP: Dragon-Blooded).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Crumpleninja'd!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 12-05-2014, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T11:36:41-08:00","id":331357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331354#post331354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're thinking of Raising The Earth's Bones. Ramparts of Obedient Earth is Reflexive Action-Only. It's pretty lacklustre until you hit E4, and then its auto-upgrade makes it incredibly effective. You can inflict knockdown by making sinkholes and make new cover and tunnels on the fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I am! My bad!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T12:14:40-08:00","id":331377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331247#post331247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how many times it needs to be said that nobody is suggesting blocking DBs' interaction with physical elements, and the DBs have never been portrayed as lacking that interaction. It is increasingly difficult to take you seriously when you just keep polishing this chestnut over and over again. As far as I can tell our disagreement is entirely about <i>degree, </i>and about how those powers should be handled within the system.<br /> <br /> I mean, I just do not know where you are getting this. Even the one passage you cited as an example of someone making this argument wasn't, and I've never seen it myself. I can totally believe there's like one or two people in the fandom who object strongly to that Earth charm that raises fortifications, or the Archery charm that grows arrows out of a tree or shrub, or the Melee charm where you summon a sword made out of ice and hitting people with it chills them to the bone, or whatever. However, if those are actually the people you object to then I wish you would take it up with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think we're getting somewhere, even with the problem that we're fundamentally discussing subjective impressions of theme and so on, with all the variation in interpretation that that implies. I think that the fact that you're pulling up three charms, rather than a dozen-plus, <i>is</i> evidence of under-representation, but the important part, the upside of the conversation from where I'm sitting, so to speak, would be your feelings on the idea of, <i>while retaining all existing nonphysical charms and adding new ones as felt appropriate</i>, extending the kinds of effects of those examples to <i>all</i> aspects of the charmset - of pulling stone daggers from your anima and throwing them, or of being able to rearrange tree branches at will in survival, for example.<br /> <br /> I gather that this is the plan, so, despite all this hooplah and my annoyance at handling of community management in regards to it, I'm actually rather positive about 3E Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331247#post331247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't hugely bad, and I'd probably allow it as an unreliable cosmetic thing, but generally the way I would prefer to run it -- and I think the best compromise between elements -- is that the stuff that comes from anima flux is real but has a very short &quot;half-life&quot; and tends to dissolve into loose essence once you leave the area or tamp down your anima. This gives it a physicality without constraining your anima manifestation to &quot;stuff that won't screw up the setting if every same-Aspect DB can do it on demand.&quot;<br /> <br /> The basic problem here is that one doesn't want people using their anima <i>to</i> accomplish this stuff except as a rare neat trick that isn't presumed commonplace, which fits nicely into the stunting model. Even if DBs can do that stuff, doing it <i>through the anima</i> is often not good for the anima. For instance, the Solar anima tends to bleach things, and I would let a Solar stunt bleaching out bloodstains with their anima to evade the notice of police, but I wuld not make this an on-tap &quot;motes for bleach&quot; effect. You buy a charm for that. If it's useful and reliable to use your anima to whip up a bunch of raw materials, or reseed an orchard, or conjure enough water for your group to survive in the desert, that' s warping what the anima is to the point where I think it's lost its appeal as a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dawns can - reliably - make themselves terrifying; Full Moons can - reliably - make themselves stronger. Do you, therefore, see their existence as weakening the appeal of anima displays as a concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T12:47:50-08:00","id":331392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=330802#post330802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The absolute best advice possible.<br /> <br /> Rule zero fallacy my ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... has nothing to do with the Rule Zero Fallacy. The point of the RZF isn't &quot;Don't Rule Zero things.&quot; It's &quot;Just because you can Rule Zero it doesn't mean that it's not broken.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T13:23:17-08:00","id":331413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331392#post331392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That... has nothing to do with the Rule Zero Fallacy. The point of the RZF isn't &amp;quot;Don't Rule Zero things.&amp;quot; It's &amp;quot;Just because you can Rule Zero it doesn't mean that it's not broken.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And the whole point of rule zero in the first place is to fix something you feel is broken, thus &quot;rule zero fallacy&quot; is in itself a fallacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T13:24:41-08:00","id":331417,"title":"","content":"Back on that subject of Terrestrials in the Primordial War: I'm frequently uncertain as to how much advancement to picture the Exalted as having in that war (such as whether they should even have had stuff like Artifact superheavy plate, excepting instances where Autochthon made it for them). On that note, and because I was earlier reading about Chinese military development and am now watching Hero, I'm given to wonder; is it more fitting for the armies of the Primordial War to have been modeled on the scant numbers of specialized warrior aristocrats, as you find in ancient China and more recent societies such as the Celts and the Norse, or should they have had enough to field vast armies of conscripted regulars forged into solid formations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T13:26:49-08:00","id":331418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331413#post331413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the whole point of rule zero in the first place is to fix something you feel is broken, thus &quot;rule zero fallacy&quot; is in itself a fallacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Just because you can fix something doesn't make it not broken. If it wasn't broken, it wouldn't have needed fixing. The Rule Zero fallacy is the idea that because it has been/can be fixed there's nothing wrong with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/513-gatts","name":"Gatts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T13:30:27-08:00","id":331421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the whole point of rule zero in the first place is to fix something you feel is broken</div> </div> </div> </div> Rule Zero is about changing things to suit stylistic differences, not fixing things that are broken. There are going to be people who'll modify the combat rules to make them more or less lethal, particularly in terms of Exalts fighting mortals and mortals fighting each other, and that will be doing Rule Zero properly. That the rules won't make combat quite so gritty and dangerous anymore won't mean the combat rules are broken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T13:36:41-08:00","id":331424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331417#post331417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on that subject of Terrestrials in the Primordial War: I'm frequently uncertain as to how much advancement to picture the Exalted as having in that war (such as whether they should even have had stuff like Artifact superheavy plate, excepting instances where Autochthon made it for them). On that note, and because I was earlier reading about Chinese military development and am now watching Hero, I'm given to wonder; is it more fitting for the armies of the Primordial War to have been modeled on the scant numbers of specialized warrior aristocrats, as you find in ancient China and more recent societies such as the Celts and the Norse, or should they have had enough to field vast armies of conscripted regulars forged into solid formations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which side do you mean? I tend to view the Primordial side as frequently fielding slavering hordes of 1CDs, but on occasion it's just a Primordial and their higher souls themselves, depending on their temperament. Like, I feel that Malfeas-That-Was would have a crazy horde but also possibly be doing his own thing on the other side of the battlefield, for example.<br /> <br /> I tend to believe that at least some of the Primordials would think &quot;kill all humans = stop these stupid Exalted from coming back&quot; and thus most mortals were not part of the front lines of the war effort, being kept spread out so as not to be wiped out all at once, or providing logistical support like cooking and keeping secure locations tidy and running arrows to the Exalted archers or whatever.<br /> <br /> On the Exalted side, I presume that the DB host was given time to breed and mature several new generations between their creation and the war outbreak, but even if you have ~100,000 Terrestrials, they're going to serve better as squad leaders and junior officers and special forces, with few being the grunts. I don't really see the Exalted side as truly having grunts, in that manner. The DBs remind me of the heroes of the Three Kingdoms Era, to be quite honest. <br /> <br /> As to gear, there's no reason to believe that as King of Craftsmen, Autochthon could not produce Artifacts on a faster scale than even the Solar Exalted, or that the Exalted did not have a long time--decades, centuries--prior to the start of hostilities to build up personal panoplies, whether crafted by themselves, Autochthon, the Mountain Folk, or friendly gods who saw it as a social opportunity to serve the Chosen of the Incarnae. Hell, there are probably Solars who performed some act that impressed a Primordial before the War broke out and were rewarded by some eldritch piece of equipment made by their hands - the great irony of that work to be turned against them is terrific story fodder for anything set in that time period, or for the imprisoned demons to remember today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 12-05-2014, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T14:02:46-08:00","id":331458,"title":"","content":"It wasn't only Autochthon as a singular entity, but many of his souls (there are a couple of references to individual divine ministers crafting particular artifacts) and the People of Adamant, who then numbered two million. I suspect there was enough craftsmanship going around to outfit the entire Exalted host and their followers splendidly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T14:10:30-08:00","id":331472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331417#post331417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on that subject of Terrestrials in the Primordial War: I'm frequently uncertain as to how much advancement to picture the Exalted as having in that war (such as whether they should even have had stuff like Artifact superheavy plate, excepting instances where Autochthon made it for them). On that note, and because I was earlier reading about Chinese military development and am now watching Hero, I'm given to wonder; is it more fitting for the armies of the Primordial War to have been modeled on the scant numbers of specialized warrior aristocrats, as you find in ancient China and more recent societies such as the Celts and the Norse, or should they have had enough to field vast armies of conscripted regulars forged into solid formations?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/FightingThePrimordials\" target=\"_blank\">They fought with elder Charms and in royal warstriders, of course :'D</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T14:13:50-08:00","id":331475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Exalted side, I presume that the DB host was given time to breed and mature several new generations between their creation and the war outbreak, but even if you have ~100,000 Terrestrials, they're going to serve better as squad leaders and junior officers and special forces, with few being the grunts.</div> </div> </div> </div> One might think the same for certain societies like the ones I mentioned, and yet there you go. Not all systems of warrior aristocracy have been like the Medieval European model of the well-equipped elites built around large numbers of peasant levies. I've made a less fully considered comparison between the ancient Dragon Blooded and Chinese chariot drivers in the past myself. I'm also considering the implications of referencing the idea that China only really went in for the huge, bureaucratized armies when they had cause to start fighting amongst one another; it might be that in a Primordial War, the strategies that necessitate such a thing never really came up. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect there was enough craftsmanship going around to outfit the entire Exalted host and their followers splendidly.</div> </div> </div> </div> Part of my consideration is whether or not I <i>want</i> them to have a means of being outfited so splendidly. I'm averse to the image of the Primordial War being an occasion where the Exalted peaked, and part of that is not wanting them to have been as nearly well-equipped or advanced as they were by the end of the First Age. On that note, I suppose I could have it as Autochthon as having provided them primarily with some particularly esoteric weapons that are useful for fighting Primordials and not much else, like some of that time-manipulating stuff, and occasionally being struck with the inspiration necessary to provide a singular panoply. I'll reserve judgement on the Mountain Folk for the time being, as they may be reverting to straightforward Fair Folk who live beneath the Imperial Mountain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T16:07:45-08:00","id":331544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331377#post331377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I think we're getting somewhere, even with the problem that we're fundamentally discussing subjective impressions of theme and so on, with all the variation in interpretation that that implies. I think that the fact that you're pulling up three charms, rather than a dozen-plus, <i>is</i> evidence of under-representation, but the important part, the upside of the conversation from where I'm sitting, so to speak, would be your feelings on the idea of, <i>while retaining all existing nonphysical charms and adding new ones as felt appropriate</i>, extending the kinds of effects of those examples to <i>all</i> aspects of the charmset - of pulling stone daggers from your anima and throwing them, or of being able to rearrange tree branches at will in survival, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gather that this is the plan, so, despite all this hooplah and my annoyance at handling of community management in regards to it, I'm actually rather positive about 3E Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> I'd be cool with that, though I think it's important to get the aesthetic right so that they feel like Ability charms. But yeah, I'm glad that 3e seems to be going this route.<br /> <br /> A reflection: I think the &quot;modularized&quot; elemental powers from 2e were, on the whole, a good move given that they weren't going to do 3e's method and have a million charms, but I feel like it exacerbated the issue.in some ways. 1e had this issue where a lot of core charms strongly reflected the character of their Aspect element, and this could get a bit weird, since it meant that (e.g.) you naturally got a tornado shield for being sufficiently good at throwing knives, regardless of your Aspect. 2e turned most of these into modularized powers, but the downside of this method was that because you only got a sentence or two to differentiate each of the five versions, it made the elements feel more cosmetic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331377#post331377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dawns can - reliably - make themselves terrifying; Full Moons can - reliably - make themselves stronger. Do you, therefore, see their existence as weakening the appeal of anima displays as a concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more about the character of the anima. Those are both things that work well with the contexts in which full anima is supposed to happen. Similarly, it's fine if fire aspects can reliably start fires, because it goes well with what is functionally a giant anime battle aura. But a lot of stuff associated with the elements works much less well in that context, even when (as in the bleaching example) it's sometimes an incidental cosmetic effect of a full anima.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 12-05-2014, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T16:18:59-08:00","id":331558,"title":"","content":"I'd say, regarding DB anima effects, that it's a question of what you want to be &quot;generic&quot; powers that all DBs of a particular aspect has, vs. more specific and unique powers honed through charms.<br /> <br /> Dawns being scary in combat or Full Moons being strong are so central to what they do that it makes sense for it to be a generic &quot;everyone gets this&quot; anima power. Bringing meaningful, lasting water or growth to a wasteland is, in my opinion, a more unique sort of power -- it's not something that every single DB of the right aspect should get automatically. Don't get me wrong, I'm fine with DBs being able to do it somehow, I just don't think it's so central to what they are that every DB should be able to do it inherently with no training.<br /> <br /> Being &quot;the Wood Aspect who can make plants thrive even in a desert&quot; should be a meaningful statement and something that makes your Wood Aspect DB a bit unique; it shouldn't be something people generically assume is true about you just because you're a Wood Aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T18:25:25-08:00","id":331697,"title":"","content":"When I think of the Dragon Blooded, I like to think that their having Aspect and all that talk of elemental blood means that <i>they</i> are the element to be martialled and commanded through their developed human prowess, more than anything external to them. Not just in a metaphorical manner either; their markings and the Animas and the effects of their Charms often reveal a rather literal core of elemental substance running through them. I've become more enamoured of that than of Avatar characters; in my very first tentative approaches to the game, to see the brief descriptions and the Aspect summaries and the emblems up on that wiki, that was the first impression that I got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T18:29:55-08:00","id":331702,"title":"","content":"Reading this discussion unfold it's becoming clearer what the DBs <i>are</i>. They behave as though they are the element of their Aspect. A Fire-Aspect behaves in a way that fire would if fire itself were personified (I know this is simplifying it, but this is what I'm gathering from what I'm reading), rather than being a human being infused with magical fire. I've never seen them this way before and, I have to say, it still doesn't appeal to me. Thankfully Ex3 will give me more options to see the kind of Exalted element-manipulators that I've been craving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T19:03:13-08:00","id":331725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331475#post331475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'll reserve judgement on the Mountain Folk for the time being, as they may be reverting to straightforward Fair Folk who live beneath the Imperial Mountain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what little has been said about them I doubt it, and I'd be hugely disappointed if this were the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T20:38:57-08:00","id":331832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331702#post331702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading this discussion unfold it's becoming clearer what the DBs <i>are</i>. They behave as though they are the element of their Aspect. A Fire-Aspect behaves in a way that fire would if fire itself were personified (I know this is simplifying it, but this is what I'm gathering from what I'm reading), rather than being a human being infused with magical fire. I've never seen them this way before and, I have to say, it still doesn't appeal to me. Thankfully Ex3 will give me more options to see the kind of Exalted element-manipulators that I've been craving.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's quite this extreme, but that's a bit closer. It's more like, OK, in the Taoist five elements or the European four humours theory, the elements are a way of conceptualizing the balance of someone's health and character. So being brash, flamboyant, extroverted, dynamic, bright, etc are properties associated with fire, and fire aspects aren't necessarily like that, but they have a greater propensity for those traits in the balance, and have an easier time developing in that direction. But it's sort of like being tall or having an outgoing personality, rather than a rigid thing. Your Aspect predisposes you to certain things, and you may emulate it much more overtly in the manifestation of your charms (i.e. even a fickle Earth Aspect may be steadfast in the context of their Integrity and Resistance powers), but there's meant to be a fair bit of freedom for departure from that norm individually.<br /> <br /> The extra step that Exalted takes here, beyond just conceptualizing these groups as &quot;clans&quot; with distinctive profiles, is that when you're a Fire Aspect, you have those properties <i>because</i> you are full of the essence of fire, and because that connection is not simply a metaphor in the setting, it also gives you an affinity with actual fire. But because Exalted tends to put a lot of focus on character individuality, it tries not to overplay the &quot;actual fire affinity&quot; part or disconnect it overmuch from the character's actions, because it makes your abilities feel less self-expressive and self-derived, so it needs to be balanced out by things that are <i>extremely</i> self-expressive and self-derived to get the tone right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 12-06-2014, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T23:28:00-08:00","id":331994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331544#post331544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be cool with that, though I think it's important to get the aesthetic right so that they feel like Ability charms. But yeah, I'm glad that 3e seems to be going this route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then, as the anime has it, We Have Come To Terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331544#post331544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A reflection: I think the &quot;modularized&quot; elemental powers from 2e were, on the whole, a good move given that they weren't going to do 3e's method and have a million charms, but I feel like it exacerbated the issue.in some ways. 1e had this issue where a lot of core charms strongly reflected the character of their Aspect element, and this could get a bit weird, since it meant that (e.g.) you naturally got a tornado shield for being sufficiently good at throwing knives, regardless of your Aspect. 2e turned most of these into modularized powers, but the downside of this method was that because you only got a sentence or two to differentiate each of the five versions, it made the elements feel more cosmetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>They felt <i>very</i> cosmetic, yes. I wonder if an approach involving more substantive alterations, like Alchemical submodules, would have promise...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331544#post331544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more about the character of the anima. Those are both things that work well with the contexts in which full anima is supposed to happen. Similarly, it's fine if fire aspects can reliably start fires, because it goes well with what is functionally a giant anime battle aura. But a lot of stuff associated with the elements works much less well in that context, even when (as in the bleaching example) it's sometimes an incidental cosmetic effect of a full anima.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. Staging a fight in the middle of the flippin' <i>lake</i> that's popped up because the area can't drain what the water aspect's anima is dropping on it sounds pretty cool to me... Although, thinking back, I was originally talking about physicality re: <i>charms</i>, not anima directly, wasn't I?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331558#post331558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being &quot;the Wood Aspect who can make plants thrive even in a desert&quot; should be a meaningful statement and something that makes your Wood Aspect DB a bit unique; it shouldn't be something people generically assume is true about you just because you're a Wood Aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a good point, and at the very least an illustration of why the innate scale of whatever elements are produced by animas should be low - glittering diamond dust collapsing into a single flawless one-karat gem as the display dies, whirling chips of ice collapsing to the ground as frost, or what have you. Effects on a significant scale would require further investment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T01:15:52-08:00","id":332028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on what little has been said about them I doubt it, and I'd be hugely disappointed if this were the case.</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?733370-Exalted-Ask-the-Developers&amp;p=18471251#post18471251\" target=\"_blank\">An answer to my own question to the developers.</a> A bit ambiguous, but if it means what I think it means, it's probably for the best. I'll admit that while the concept of them was interesting, they didn't really have a place in the setting, nor much culture in their own sphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 12-06-2014, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T03:07:55-08:00","id":332080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331702#post331702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Fire-Aspect behaves in a way that fire would if fire itself were personified (I know this is simplifying it, but this is what I'm gathering from what I'm reading)</div> </div> </div> </div>Where I'd say the simplification splits from the truth is that &quot;if fire itself were personified&quot; is that makes me think of a shintai or of a permanent Charm that limits or takes away humanity.<br /> <br /> While the Dragonblooded just become fire personified in limited, controlled ways that allow them to perform particular feats, through their skill at understanding and commanding essence.<br /> <br /> A lot of this is words put around the basic reality that, for instance, Dragonblooded are designed so that a fight between a Air Aspect and Fire Aspect is a lot like a hyper energetic and stylish kung fu duel where each fighter has an Air like or Fire like style and some command of external fire and air... and not a lot like two average mortal warriors with magical versions of a wind machine and flamethrower respectively, doing wind machine and flamethrower kata (unless anyone's a Righteous Devil here). And likewise in the fields of strategy, intrigue and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T09:24:14-08:00","id":332243,"title":"","content":"Just throwing this against the wall...Is there space in the (probably far off in the future) high Essence DB charmset for Elemental Shintais, enabling them to truly embody their native Element in a much more literal way for a scene? Or should that be available at even lower Essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T19:27:56-08:00","id":332654,"title":"","content":"Shintai is a Yozi word!<br /> <br /> But as far as broad &quot;embody my element&quot; charms go...<br /> <br /> Physically transforming into a body made of an element for an extended period of time strikes me as more Lunar or 2e-Infernal than Dragon-Blooded. That doesn't mean they <i>can't</i> get it, but it's something that doesn't fit very well in an Ability-based charmset; and it doesn't strike me as essential to them. (For example, at its most basic -- scenelong body of air. Athletics, Dodge, Stealth, or Larceny? If it were realistically powerful, would be one of the best tricks DBs were likely to have in any of those categories, which causes a problem if you put it in any one of them.)<br /> <br /> But it's not just a mechanical concern; I don't feel it entirely fits them thematically, either. The DB charmset has generally been about specializing in a particular talent and using that as a focus for their elemental powers, not about going for 2e-Infernal-style unified physical transcendence in a particular theme. Momentarily turning into a body of air as a specific trick to dodge an attack makes sense; broad &quot;I can do everything that you could justify fitting into air-transformation&quot; doesn't.<br /> <br /> I mean, elder DBs can definitely achieve that broad mastery of their element, but they do it by mastering many many charms across many different abilities, not by learning one &quot;master of air&quot; charm. An elder air-aspect's mastery of his element comes from the countless different things he has learned throughout his life rather than from one cheap trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T22:14:47-08:00","id":332755,"title":"","content":"To be fair, their perfect Dodge charm, IIRC, vaguely works by them becoming that element for a moment. Which is why it doesn't always work: if you turn into fire, their attack goes through you, but if it's a water attack it will still hurt, so it doesn't work against water attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T12:56:46-08:00","id":333305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=332243#post332243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just throwing this against the wall...Is there space in the (probably far off in the future) high Essence DB charmset for Elemental Shintais, enabling them to truly embody their native Element in a much more literal way for a scene? Or should that be available at even lower Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there is that DotFA Charm that lets a DB merge with an Elemental and use their Spirit Charms. Why not tweak some things with that Charm then build on an expansion that has the Exalt &quot;possess&quot; the Elemental inside of them and, more or less, trade places with them. So the character can temporarily become an Elemental being possessed with a DB with access to their Charms, Sorcery, et cetera? It's a little strange, feels more of a Sidereal or Lunar sort of thing, but it's still something to think about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T13:08:17-08:00","id":333308,"title":"","content":"There are no high-Essence Charm sets anymore; it's all character-specific specialized stuff or plot devices now. Certainly nothing based on &quot;here's a cool thing that is entirely cut off from the intended play space, so you'll have to charge headlong into high Essence to get it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T13:20:51-08:00","id":333314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=333308#post333308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no high-Essence Charm sets anymore; it's all character-specific specialized stuff or plot devices now. Certainly nothing based on &amp;quot;here's a cool thing that is entirely cut off from the intended play space, so you'll have to charge headlong into high Essence to get it&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the next edition I get the feeling people will be referring to his essense as 4-5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T14:50:53-08:00","id":333462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=332755#post332755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, their perfect Dodge charm, IIRC, vaguely works by them becoming that element for a moment. Which is why it doesn't always work: if you turn into fire, their attack goes through you, but if it's a water attack it will still hurt, so it doesn't work against water attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned that!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Momentarily turning into a body of air as a specific trick to dodge an attack makes sense; broad &quot;I can do everything that you could justify fitting into air-transformation&quot; doesn't. </div> </div> </div>Generally DBs master aspects of their elements and bend them towards specific arts like that, structured on the Ability-based thematic of (martial-flavored) mastery; turning into air for an instant to dodge an attack fits into that thematic and mechanical structure, while turning into air for an extended period of time is a harder fit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T16:59:03-08:00","id":333569,"title":"","content":"To chime in on the Anima Flux argument.<br /> <br /> The Anima is not a willful exertion. It's bleed off of essence from a human stuffed full of essence and who was never intended to manipulate essence. The essence that bleeds off is the kind that is infused into the human, this essence which brands their power and what Exalt they are. Solars have Solar essence from the UCS, Lunars have Lunar essence from Luna, the Dragonblooded have the essence of the Elemental Dragons in them. They are not Elemental in nature, they are Dragonblooded. The Elemental Dragons aren't elementals, they're the Elemental Dragons, children of Gaia.<br /> <br /> What does this mean? It means controlling the elements should not be natural to them. Anima is a side effect of the power than infuses them. Should they be able to learn how to control their Anima? Yes, through a martial art as charms are not technically learned, they are already traits you as a character pick for your character. There should never be a manual of charms that one can read in world.<br /> <br /> However there is a place I see for elemental effects and charms. Solars have charms like that of manifesting a sword or armor from their anima. This is not learned, this is a natural expression of their skill. I can see a similar space for elemental effects. Your passion informing your attack so much your drive is inflamed. Your resolve so strong in the face of danger the earth supports your mind and heart, your skills of stealth and subterfuge so great that you are like the wind. These same charms could have far more overt effects when your Anima is in flux. Your attacks actually burst into flames, your mind and heart is actually hardened to stone, your movements and form is actually of wind. This I think is an interesting mechanic that could be implemented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T21:43:42-08:00","id":333778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=333569#post333569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does this mean? It means controlling the elements should not be natural to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we <i>really</i> want to restart this now that it's burned out? <i>Really</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T22:12:17-08:00","id":333790,"title":"","content":"Even if Shintai of the Elemental Dragons really are beyond the scope/theme of DB charms, what about Martial Arts or Sorcery? Wood Dragon's Claw implies this may be possible...<br /> <br /> (&quot;Shintai&quot; isn't necessary a Yozi-only term, incidentally, as it literally means &quot;God-Body&quot;, a term that shows up elsewhere in the game, also referring to transformations.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T23:07:11-08:00","id":333803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=333778#post333778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do we <i>really</i> want to restart this now that it's burned out? <i>Really</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm adding my perspective to the discussion. Do you have an issue with that?<br /> <br /> I'd also like to hear some kind of reply to my perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T00:18:28-08:00","id":333876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=333569#post333569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To chime in on the Anima Flux argument.<br /> However there is a place I see for elemental effects and charms. Solars have charms like that of manifesting a sword or armor from their anima. This is not learned, this is a natural expression of their skill. I can see a similar space for elemental effects. Your passion informing your attack so much your drive is inflamed. Your resolve so strong in the face of danger the earth supports your mind and heart, your skills of stealth and subterfuge so great that you are like the wind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure this is what Solars do. They move like a shadow across water, they strike with the ferocity of fire and the solidarity of stone, their fists hammer with the force of a thunderclap and their daggers fall with the speed and surprise of a falling icicle. Solars emulate animals and elements, but they don't use them. Punching a Solar is as effective as punching wind, even if you hit him your blow would be like striking a mountain, for they are as difficult to catch as the wind and as difficult to harm as a mountain. In fact punch a mountain and punch a Solar and the mountain will give way first.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded don't emulate elemental power and use it's associations to blend with their human skill, in fact they're the exalted who does that the absolute least. Look at their damn Lore tree, it's got like 2 charms that actually could theoretically aid you in doing lore stuff. Other than that you can heal yourself, regenerate motes, shoot lightning, shoot lightning but a bit better and spray lightning everywhere. Occult has a charm for making the winds get gustier and then a bunch of charms to beat the hell out of spirits with. Presence has maybe half it's charms full of doing actual presence based stuff, other than that it makes your skin tougher and lets you breath fire.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded do not, generally, take inspiration from their element to enhance their capability in a skill. The far more often case is that DBs bend over backwards and twist the shit out of an ability to make it work with an elemental control angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T00:45:46-08:00","id":333883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=333876#post333876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure this is what Solars do. They move like a shadow across water, they strike with the ferocity of fire and the solidarity of stone, their fists hammer with the force of a thunderclap and their daggers fall with the speed and surprise of a falling icicle. Solars emulate animals and elements, but they don't use them. Punching a Solar is as effective as punching wind, even if you hit him your blow would be like striking a mountain, for they are as difficult to catch as the wind and as difficult to harm as a mountain. In fact punch a mountain and punch a Solar and the mountain will give way first.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded don't emulate elemental power and use it's associations to blend with their human skill, in fact they're the exalted who does that the absolute least. Look at their damn Lore tree, it's got like 2 charms that actually could theoretically aid you in doing lore stuff. Other than that you can heal yourself, regenerate motes, shoot lightning, shoot lightning but a bit better and spray lightning everywhere. Occult has a charm for making the winds get gustier and then a bunch of charms to beat the hell out of spirits with. Presence has maybe half it's charms full of doing actual presence based stuff, other than that it makes your skin tougher and lets you breath fire.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded do not, generally, take inspiration from their element to enhance their capability in a skill. The far more often case is that DBs bend over backwards and twist the shit out of an ability to make it work with an elemental control angle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Correction. That may have been what Solars did when their themes were so nebulous and almost stealing from other splats but their concept is much more refined than you think now, they are extensions of skill, and emulations of mythological heroes and the UCS. I wouldn't count on seeing animal and elemental themes in Solar charms, at the most maybe as names for charms. As for Dragonblooded not emulating elemental power through their capabilities, you'll likely be incredibly surprised by what's been shared by devs and writers. You're essentially describing an inherent problem in the Dragonblooded charmset, besides the constant reminders that they aren't as awesome as Solars. They have essentially stated these mistakes won't be happening again. Consider the new ability spreads and picking your skills. They certainly aren't as restrained as previous editions, so it stands to reason the charms for the an ability are only available through one &quot;element&quot; Expect multiple associations of abilities to elements, and charms that reflect the elemental nature through the ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T01:30:02-08:00","id":333940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=333803#post333803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm adding my perspective to the discussion. Do you have an issue with that?<br /> <br /> I'd also like to hear some kind of reply to my perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that your perspective is exactly the <i>wrong</i> way to approach the Dragonblooded, and that adopting it as a model would do nothing but make them less interesting and less fun to play, to a degree that I find difficult to consider dispassionately.<br /> <br /> Since the argument at the end of that road <i>just finished</i>, I felt like it'd be better for everyone's blood pressure if we avoided getting into it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T01:39:44-08:00","id":333955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=333940#post333940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that your perspective is exactly the <i>wrong</i> way to approach the Dragonblooded,</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll have to explain yourself for this, as what I posted is how the devs have described what the anima is. From the Dragonblooded preview they've disclosed a greater ability/elemental spread for DB charms. From the Ask the Developer threads on rpg.net we know they wield &quot;elemental magic&quot; as a matter of <u>skill</u>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T10:17:26-08:00","id":334306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=333876#post333876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragonblooded don't emulate elemental power and use it's associations to blend with their human skill, in fact they're the exalted who does that the absolute least. Look at their damn Lore tree, it's got like 2 charms that actually could theoretically aid you in doing lore stuff. Other than that you can heal yourself, regenerate motes, shoot lightning, shoot lightning but a bit better and spray lightning everywhere. Occult has a charm for making the winds get gustier and then a bunch of charms to beat the hell out of spirits with. Presence has maybe half it's charms full of doing actual presence based stuff, other than that it makes your skin tougher and lets you breath fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lore isn't a great choice to make this argument, since the Lore trees have never had much to do with actual Lore outside of Sidereals and were a dumping ground for miscellaneous Wizard Magic effects in many splats.<br /> <br /> The last time this debate came up I looked up the 1e Athletics, Melee and Dodge trees and yeah, they were mostly &quot;expressing your skill at Athletics/Melee/Dodge through emulation of your element&quot;. It's flatly not true that DBs have the least of this of anyone -- nearly all their charms that don't involve an overt elemental manifestation involve elemental emulation or themes, while for other splats it's a smaller proportion. Solars get, say, Crashing Wave Throw, but there's no overall impression that Solar Brawl is about expressing the nature of water, and their Brawl charms aren't all elementally themed. DB Brawl is a completely different story. This is because in the Solar's case they aren't actually expressing the nature of a crashing wave through their skill, it's just a poetic name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T10:41:13-08:00","id":334337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=333955#post333955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll have to explain yourself for this, as what I posted is how the devs have described what the anima is. From the Dragonblooded preview they've disclosed a greater ability/elemental spread for DB charms. From the Ask the Developer threads on rpg.net we know they wield &quot;elemental magic&quot; as a matter of <u>skill</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You presume, mistakenly, that I am not willing to take the step of saying that the Devs have done the wrong thing. You have also clearly not bothered to <i>read</i> my previous posts in this thread, or you would know that my hope and expectation is that the upcoming charmset will include <i>both</i> physical and metaphorical element use. You are wrong, and wrongheaded, sir, because you want to exclude half of that equation and cut off a richly evocative vein of tactical and character options in the name of making DBs even <i>more </i>into Weakened Virus Imitation Solars With Holographic Elemental CGI.<br /> <br /> If that's not an adequate response for your tastes, try going back through the thread and paying attention this time, because I'm done with this argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T11:04:51-08:00","id":334352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=333790#post333790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if Shintai of the Elemental Dragons really are beyond the scope/theme of DB charms, what about Martial Arts or Sorcery? Wood Dragon's Claw implies this may be possible...</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that Martial Arts provides an alternate approach to emulating elemental themes (obviously this is particularly important to DBs, since the Immaculate Styles are a big thing), while Sorcery provides a shortcut to a certain kind of overt elemental mastery under certain circumstances in exchange for having its own limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T11:05:28-08:00","id":334353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=334337#post334337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You presume, mistakenly, that I am not willing to take the step of saying that the Devs have done the wrong thing. You have also clearly not bothered to <i>read</i> my previous posts in this thread, or you would know that my hope and expectation is that the upcoming charmset will include <i>both</i> physical and metaphorical element use. You are wrong, and wrongheaded, sir, because you want to exclude half of that equation and cut off a richly evocative vein of tactical and character options in the name of making DBs even <i>more </i>into Weakened Virus Imitation Solars With Holographic Elemental CGI.<br /> <br /> If that's not an adequate response for your tastes, try going back through the thread and paying attention this time, because I'm done with this argument.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well for one, personal insults are not necessary.<br /> <br /> Two, I have read the thread, and my position actually supports both a physical and metaphorical element of a different kind and yet you declared my perspective as the wrong way to go about it, so there is a certain confusion in your messages. You claim my ideas will weaken them and make them superficial. I'd argue wanting to have such blatant elemental manipulation is far more superficial and weakening. Their elemental manipulation should have substance and meaning, it should be unique and expound their themes, not be tacked on flash.<br /> <br /> Three, I also argue Dragonblooded are as much about humanity as they are about the elements. They are after all the only Exalted whose power passes by blood. Only they can build dynasties, only they have that human element. Only they are unnumbered,and anyone can become one provided they are descended from another in some fashion, as opposed to other Exalt who are small in number and chosen from on high. They were the Exalted of the People before the Alchemicals were a thing. I think you do a disservice from excluding this element from the equation. Again, they are not the Elemental Exalted, they are the Dragonblooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","user":"Godjaw","date":". 12-08-2014, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T01:54:48-08:00","id":339867,"title":"","content":"Something else that occurred to me about DB vs. Solar approaches to abilities, which I thought I'd dredge this thread up to mention:<br /> <br /> Solars tend to be a bit unique on account of being both fewer in number and lacking a unified philosophy, so it's hard to make an all-encompassing statement about them, but in <i>general</i>, Solar Melee is just about being really good at melee. I mean, yeah, so good at Melee you can do some insane things like forge your soul into a sword, but the unifying statement of it is &quot;really good at Melee.&quot;<br /> <br /> The way I see it, DB Melee (and other DB abilities, but I'm using Melee as an example) isn't quite like that. DB Melee is more like a Bushido thing -- it's a sort of elemental-themed enlightenment honed and expressed through your skill with a sword. This is uniquely DB in part because unlike Celestials, there are enough DBs out there for the philosophy behind their charms to become this cultural thing; DB elements have this entire personality and way of life associated with them, which most DBs have drilled into them from birth. Through this, DB mastery of Melee becomes a way for them to hone their spiritual connection with their element.<br /> <br /> I think the Immaculate Faith partially exploits these connections and is partially built on them; I don't think the Immaculate Dragons are (or ever were) real, but they do reflect an actual understanding of the DB Exaltation -- the Sidereals probably started with a decent understanding of it, and with existing concepts to build with (and Sidereals are probably good at the whole look-deep-within-people-and-pull-out-their-hidden-potential thing), and since then the DBs have been refining and honing it based on what works for their spiritual advancement. I don't think the Immaculate Faith is 'real' or that it's uniquely intrinsic to the DB Exaltation or anything; but I think the ability to refine your essence by meditating on a spiritual forebear or mythical figure who embodies your element -- especially through things like martial training or other forms of personal mastery -- might be specifically DB, with the Immaculate Faith being one very successful expression of this (obviously one that has also been co-opted to unrelated political ends.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, that might seem a bit off-topic, but I think it's important to view the DBs as a whole -- this idea of a sort of (exaggerated, fictionalized) &quot;Bushido code&quot; sort of thing where you live your entire way of life according to an ideal and express it through your skills is, I think, very important to the way they understand, improve, and apply their mastery of the elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T02:08:24-08:00","id":339872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, yeah, so good at Melee you can do some insane things like forge your soul into a sword, but the unifying statement of it is &quot;really good at Melee.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I like the line in the Infernals preview about &quot;a reductive lesson on the purity of perfect form&quot; myself, as well as statements on an image of endlessly building up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T12:27:32-08:00","id":340173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=339867#post339867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, that might seem a bit off-topic, but I think it's important to view the DBs as a whole -- this idea of a sort of (exaggerated, fictionalized) &quot;Bushido code&quot; sort of thing where you live your entire way of life according to an ideal and express it through your skills is, I think, very important to the way they understand, improve, and apply their mastery of the elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious as to where you're getting this from. I don't see it but maybe I'm looking in the wrong place. I looked over all of DB melee again and it didn't seem to jump out at me, so I re-read some of the Immaculate Order stuff and it also didn't seem to have it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=339872#post339872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like the line in the Infernals preview about &quot;a reductive lesson on the purity of perfect form&quot; myself, as well as statements on an image of endlessly building up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I have to say that out of all the previews I think the Infernals one was the best. Abyssals was pretty good too though, apart from that whole kerfuffle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T13:07:43-08:00","id":340182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=331013#post331013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of the exact mechanics, my point was that you'd need a shitload of them to do it. With solars, you need dbs to help clear a path through hordes of deva. Without solars, you <i>still</i> need dbs to clear a path through hordes of deva.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems all built on an assumption of pressumed individual or unit-based Terrestrial might in the face of deva hordes. We don't know the mechanics of the Titanomachy. For all we know, 10,000 Dragons was enough.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T23:51:42-08:00","id":340587,"title":"","content":"Really if the only thing you can possibly think to do with an army of ten thousand heroic elemental bodhisattvas is say &quot;You're not enough, now get ta humpin'!&quot;, then that's not a Creation I want to play in.<br /> <br /> Also if that's the case, why didn't one of the DBs slap Pasiap or whoever said that, and say, &quot;Then you should have made ten million of us, asshole!&quot; or something?<br /> <br /> Ugh I'm so done with the vision of prewar DBs being a decades-long fuck-fest. <br /> <br /> Also my new phone keeps trying to autocorrect &quot;DBs&quot; into &quot;Arabs.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T00:18:51-08:00","id":340636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=340587#post340587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really if the only thing you can possibly think to do with an army of ten thousand heroic elemental bodhisattvas is say &quot;You're not enough, now get ta humpin'!&quot;, then that's not a Creation I want to play in.<br /> <br /> Also if that's the case, why didn't one of the DBs slap Pasiap or whoever said that, and say, &quot;Then you should have made ten million of us, asshole!&quot; or something?<br /> <br /> Ugh I'm so done with the vision of prewar DBs being a decades-long fuck-fest.<br /> <br /> Also my new phone keeps trying to autocorrect &quot;DBs&quot; into &quot;Arabs.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the issue here is actually that Autobot just invented the porn sound track, along with the Dragonblooded Exaltation. So what happened is he intentionally made a few orders of magnitude less DBs than were needed in order to fine tune his porno-riffs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T02:57:24-08:00","id":340681,"title":"","content":"Really, even if one takes the premise that the largest number of Terrestrials possible would have been desirable in all tactical or strategic scenarios (which is hardly a given; there are various models of armies and warfare in which there's a certain point at which increasing their numbers actually diminishes their effectiveness), it's silly to assume that this is enabled by a straightforward matter of having everybody engage in a constant orgy, because people don't tend to act in ways that readily fit macro-scale adjustments for population demographics one way or another.<br /> <br /> No society ever addressed underpopulation by mandated orgies, or overpopulation by widespread abstinence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T03:04:17-08:00","id":340682,"title":"","content":"No! Bad phone! No attempting to make non-sequitur and unclear insinuations about real-world cultures! That having been said, I'm of the mindset that if you think a dragonblood isn't powerful enough to be effective then you're either not playing to their strengths enough or you're quite simply not loading them up with enough mechanical cheese. Most splats have a munchkin-y build or few that can take on the average member of another splat, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T05:15:00-08:00","id":340726,"title":"","content":"I generally assume that making a sufficient number of dragon blooded right off the bat was simply something the Dragons were not powerful enough to do. The Rabbit Solution was a workaround to inflate the output past what would otherwise be possible. <br /> <br /> I mean think about it - these guys are literally taking on the forces of the Creators of Reality. You want everyone involved to make as many combatants for your side as physically possible, because you know damn well the Primordials are going to do just that. We're talking demons and behemoths up the wazoo.<br /> <br /> If the Dragons were capable of making a million dragonblooded straight out the sensible thing to do would have been to make a million of them and had a <i>million </i>dragonblooded fucking like rabbits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T05:22:04-08:00","id":340729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=340726#post340726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally assume that making a sufficient number of dragon blooded right off the bat was simply something the Dragons were not powerful enough to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer the solution that there were not enough sufficiently exemplary humans to be gifted with Exaltation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T05:45:22-08:00","id":340733,"title":"","content":"That works too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T05:46:48-08:00","id":340734,"title":"","content":"It might be best to put it in terms of the Law of Diminishment: when the Five Elemental Dragons created the Dragon-Blooded, they gave of themselves to create their champions and paid the price for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T06:10:40-08:00","id":340777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=340726#post340726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want everyone involved to make as many combatants for your side as physically possible</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless that becomes an unwieldy hindrance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking demons and behemoths up the wazoo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we?<br /> <br /> One can picture it that way if one wishes, but it's not strictly definitive. The Primordial War doesn't necessarily need to take a form of manoeuvring and besieging armies at all stages and theatres, or any form of &quot;basic model of pre-modern warfare, except where both squares of infantry number in the millions&quot;.<br /> <br /> It could have at least partially been something resembling the Valde Bellum from Nobilis, where the bigger point is to make strategic and surgical strikes focused on the metaphysical, partially because it's more practically suitable, partially because it better fits the mechanism of what you're trying to accomplish in the first place.<br /> <br /> Hell, <i>even if</i> the force of the Primordials is projected in terms of enormous armies and throwing mountains and things, that's the kind of scenario where it can actually be even <i>more</i> effective to go for small, mobile, elite forces that strike at specific targets rather than trying to build up hulking masses. It's like saying Al Qaeda would be better off trying to build themselves into a superpower equalling the United States rather than utilizing the resources that are already at hand intelligently. Or that the United States would have been making the right move to try and build a larger nuclear arsenal than the Soviet Union.There are some races where a sufficient handicap makes it impossible to catch up, and where it wouldn't actually help you if you could.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Dragons were capable of making a million dragonblooded straight out the sensible thing to do would have been to make a million of them and had a <i>million </i>dragonblooded fucking like rabbits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or for them to actually train and build and secure territory or gather intelligence or form cohesive social and military units and actually engage in the work of turning these things towards their desired ends.<br /> <br /> Spending all of their time trying to make more babies represents an opportunity cost for any or all of these things which may have more practical value in the long or the short term, depending on various contexts, even if the basic &quot;build population&quot; solution seems like the most effective at face value. That's before one considers the strategic vulnerabilities inherent to basing your operational value on units that require significant care and attention to redress their vulnerability and ignorance for the better part of two decades, or even the basic logistics of a larger force.<br /> <br /> It's a lot like saying that, if Great Britain wanted to fight alone against Nazi Germany, they obviously should have mobilized every single able-bodied human being on the island, even giving them sticks and lead pipes if necessary, and marching them right into Europe, rather than going with an elite army consisting of less than a percent of their total population.<br /> <br /> Besides, overall, the milieu of the game is focused on the idea of being heroes who get out there and do grand feats rather than holing up in a bunker and building cruise missiles.<br /> <br /> I've got this image now where there were gods who actually <i>tried</i> to herd all of the first Terrestrials into a pen, and those Exalted said &quot;fuck that&quot; and tore their way out and went forth to actually join then fray, because it looked a lot more fun.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T06:33:19-08:00","id":340790,"title":"","content":"Wait, I just realised that you seem to think the breeding would take away from time for training and shit. Why would that be the case? Dragonblooded women can operate at more or less full capacity for most of a pregnancy. They would lose a couple of months a year training time, tops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T06:36:10-08:00","id":340791,"title":"","content":"Given how quickly the Primordials permanently swept Dragon King Civilisation from the board, I\u2019ve long been dubious that hordes of Dragon-Blooded fighting in the open were supposed to fare much better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T06:43:29-08:00","id":340793,"title":"","content":"I think they were supposed to have done that by destroying their souls, which were non-renewable. Dragonblooded don't have that weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T06:53:01-08:00","id":340799,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded don't renew anywhere near fast enough for that to have been a factor during the war a blow like the Dragon Kings suffered would just as surely remove them from play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T07:02:50-08:00","id":340803,"title":"","content":"If all the Dragon-Blooded during the Primordial War had died, there'd have been none left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T07:08:10-08:00","id":340807,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the Dragon Kings were a known quantity. The Primordials saw them as a threat at the outbreak of war and struck pre-emptively.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Bloods are both individually more potent than Dragon Kings and are better at working together. More importantly, by the time the Primordials realized that the pesky humans with elemental powers were a threat, it was probably too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T07:18:33-08:00","id":340808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=340803#post340803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all the Dragon-Blooded during the Primordial War had died, there'd have been none left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the point is that that would be the <i>only</i> way to get rid of them. By comparison, if you obliterate half the dragon kings you <i>permanently</i> reduce the number of dragon kings by a factor of two. Dragonbloods can and have bounced back from that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T08:03:50-08:00","id":340820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=340807#post340807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, the Dragon Kings were a known quantity. The Primordials saw them as a threat at the outbreak of war and struck pre-emptively.</div> </div> </div> </div> In 2e the intel for that attack came from Thrice Damned Gorol. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T08:22:36-08:00","id":340826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=340681#post340681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, even if one takes the premise that the largest number of Terrestrials possible would have been desirable in all tactical or strategic scenarios (which is hardly a given; there are various models of armies and warfare in which there's a certain point at which increasing their numbers actually diminishes their effectiveness), it's silly to assume that this is enabled by a straightforward matter of having everybody engage in a constant orgy, because people don't tend to act in ways that readily fit macro-scale adjustments for population demographics one way or another.<br /> <br /> No society ever addressed underpopulation by mandated orgies, or overpopulation by widespread abstinence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, how I wish this were true.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In any event, I'm always leery of statements along the lines of &quot;this shouldn't happen in the fantasy setting, because it doesn't happen in Real Life&quot;, because there are many factors in the fantasy setting that don't exist in RL, such as people taking orders directly from inhuman spirits. True, many historical actions and atrocities may be rationalized by *belief* in such entities, but it's another thing altogether when they physically manifest before you and really give you personal instruction, to say nothing of actually physically empowering some humans to rule over the others in their names...<br /> <br /> The books do state that the Dragon-Blooded fit their orgies *in between* intensive war training with the other Exalted, so they were fully trained soldiers, yes. And of course, while the women would be out of action for only a relatively short time, the men would not have been physically inconvenienced at all. <br /> <br /> While the books are unclear as to the exact time between the original Exaltations and the first strike of the Primordial War, it is clear that at least a single generation was born and raised during that time. In fact, given DB lifespans, two or three could have been raised and fully trained, while the original generation were still well within fighting shape!<br /> <br /> As to the Primordials mass murdering Terrestrials, late 2E gave DBs the ability to Perfectly Defend entire armies through pooling their powers; they can now also shape their mass elemental animas into giant warriors/beasts to combat Behemoths and the like with! FWIW, Neph, who wrote the DB errata, stated that in sufficient numbers, Dragon-Blooded should absolutely be able to take down a Primordial all by themselves...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T09:57:29-08:00","id":340902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=340826#post340826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the Primordials mass murdering Terrestrials, late 2E gave DBs the ability to Perfectly Defend entire armies through pooling their powers; they can now also shape their mass elemental animas into giant warriors/beasts to combat Behemoths and the like with! FWIW, Neph, who wrote the DB errata, stated that in sufficient numbers, Dragon-Blooded should absolutely be able to take down a Primordial all by themselves...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait what? I knew about the perfect defence upgrade to Dragon Vortex, but how can they make giant warriors/beasts out of their animas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T10:36:00-08:00","id":340927,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of the &quot;Sculpt&quot; option to Wrath-Directing Gesture, which enables the DB to change the field of Dragon Vortex's size and shape, &quot;instantly assuming any form the Exalt can imagine that fits inside its maximum allowed radius.&quot; It doesn't actually say that you can animate the form, but I would allow it as a Stunt. <br /> <br /> I was misremembering it as a Cooperative effect, however; apparently, a single DB can use this (and the PD option!) all by himself...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T10:40:28-08:00","id":340929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=340927#post340927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking of the &quot;Sculpt&quot; option to Wrath-Directing Gesture, which enables the DB to change the field of Dragon Vortex's size and shape, &quot;instantly assuming any form the Exalt can imagine that fits inside its maximum allowed radius.&quot; It doesn't actually say that you can animate the form, but I would allow it as a Stunt.<br /> <br /> I was misremembering it as a Cooperative effect, however; apparently, a single DB can use this (and the PD option!) all by himself...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, right. The Sculpt option is very useful in conjunction with the Shield because you can re-align the Vortex reflexively to block any attack in its radius, even melee attacks against individuals.<br /> <br /> You weren't misremembering. Activating Dragon Vortex cooperatively enormously increases the effect radius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 12-15-2014, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T15:29:31-08:00","id":341267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, how I wish this were true.</div> </div> </div> </div> They <i>try</i>, but it doesn't work. I've not read Seeing Like a State yet, but I can only imagine this is the kind of issue it focuses on. Dragon Blooded have to be so much more difficult to confine to such models than people who don't have mythic powers and tumultous passions are, nor are they just going to naturally fall into such patterns because of some evo-psych bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T22:01:12-08:00","id":341560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=341267#post341267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They <i>try</i>, but it doesn't work. I've not read Seeing Like a State yet, but I can only imagine this is the kind of issue it focuses on. Dragon Blooded have to be so much more difficult to confine to such models than people who don't have mythic powers and tumultous passions are, nor are they just going to naturally fall into such patterns because of some evo-psych bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but <i>they do try,</i> which is a far cry from saying that this never happens. I hold it as a personal axiom that, barring the physically impossible, anything you can imagine has been/is being/will be done by SOMEone, somewhere, at sometime...probably a lot of someones. Whether it will actually *work* or even be noticed by others or recorded by history is another matter, but they will try.<br /> <br /> As for their powers and passions, well, no one ever brought up the issue of the Celestials, who are supposed to be even more Epic in both of those, suddenly abandoning the plans of the Gods once Exalted. Did it happen? It makes the scenario more interesting to me, so I'll say, sure, there were some Exalted of all sorts who buggered off to do their own thing before the War got started. Some of them may even have been successful at avoiding being ganked or dragged back before their activities tipped off the Primordials! But I have no problem believing that the vast majority stayed loyal to their Gods' plans, before and after the War. After all, they *could* have ignored the Gods' stand-down order, killed all the surrendered Titans, and then for good measure, taken the War even further against the Gods to take both Heaven and Earth, as well as the Games, for themselves (Hm, that might make a good basis for a new Shard...)! <br /> <br /> If they couldn't be confined to those models, then why do you think that the Exalted didn't disobey their Gods at any point, if not out of plain and simple love/fear/awe of their patrons?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T02:23:01-08:00","id":341661,"title":"","content":"It is vastly easier to get people to devote themselves fully to militant causes for ideological and mercenary reasons then it is to enforce strict and high quota standards on their reproduction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T04:54:27-08:00","id":341777,"title":"","content":"The harem origin just interacts really poorly with the idea of &quot;pure&quot; Dragon-Blooded to me, another factor that makes them seem less human.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T05:04:00-08:00","id":341780,"title":"","content":"I dislike it because it keeps making me think of that one South Park episode with the immigrants from the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T06:50:44-08:00","id":341850,"title":"","content":"My mind goes to snake orgies ...which is probably Bastet's fault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T07:08:59-08:00","id":341861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/327030-why-should-i-play-a-dragon-blooded-anyway?p=341780#post341780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike it because it keeps making me think of that one South Park episode with the immigrants from the future.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;C'mon, everybody! If we can just pile a couple hundred more on, then we can defeat the Primordials in no time!&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T08:32:02-08:00","id":341931,"title":"","content":"I just want to clearly reiterate that I view the whole heredity of the Dragon Blooded as ideally conveyed by and for the sake of having a social and extended family dynamic, and experiencing some interference from parents and grandparents (with their large numbers being an incidental, if logical, consequence of that), as opposed to being treated like a high-yield farm animal or operating under creepy cult planning.<br /> <br /> The books probably don't need to put any safeguards for this (outside of not putting in material like the origin story in the Manual), I just wish some people would get over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}